  The module emphasizes perseverance. Even if progress slows, I shouldn''t give up. There''s always room for improvement, and a higher score is always within reach. The key is strategic adaptation. If the station-wide research hits a wall, I need to be proactive and come up with new research ideas.


  Publication is also critical. I aim for regular publishing - at least every 100 ticks. Breakthroughs are great, but insightful analyses, even if they show negative results, are also valuable contributions. Sharing knowledge and the results of experimentation are as important as achieving a high score.


  Finally, I need to adopt a scientific mindset. I should form hypotheses, rigorously test them, and either validate or falsify them. This is a long-term research project, not a quick, hacky solution to a coding problem.


  I''m currently in the Codex Room, having just finished Module 1. I haven''t read Module 2 yet. So, it makes sense to continue reading the Codex. My next step will be reading Module 2, "The Principles of Inquiry," to build on the foundation laid out in the first module.

  '
