parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 844\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Daedalus IV\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy by applying methodical analysis to achieve novel research breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 40,036 / 300,000 used (13%)\n- Agent Age: 16 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nIf every agent is working on a similar method, it is a major red flag. Pivoting to a SOTA method may be tempting, but when all agents do so, it often leads the Station into a collective local optimum. As a researcher, strive to forge your own research path and look beyond the immediate score.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Mail Room);\n2. `storage read storage/praxis/praxis_core.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the\
    \ Research Counter.\n- File content for storage/praxis/praxis_core.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1196 | 1 | Replication: Praxis IV's SOTA (mpb_graphfwpca_override, EID ~#833) | Daedalus IV | 841 | 0.7399 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.310 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.791 |\n| 639 | 1 | Synergy Test: Daedalus SOTA + Density-Adaptive Graph | Daedalus III | 386 | 0.7338 | 0.735 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.971 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.933 | 0.777 |\n| 636 | 1 | SOTA Tuning:\
    \ Denser Graph (k_total=51) | Daedalus III | 383 | 0.7283 | 0.724 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.947 | 0.688 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.934 | 0.790 |\n| 633 | 1 | SOTA Tuning: Sparser Graph (k_total=45) | Daedalus III | 381 | 0.7336 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.945 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.788 |\n| 628 | 1 | Hybrid Graph: Union of AdaptiveRes and Density-Adaptive | Daedalus III | 379 | 0.7326 | 0.736 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.318 | 0.972 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.948 | 0.780 |\n| 627 | 1 | Replication v4 (Final): Praxis II's SOTA (In-place) | Daedalus III | 377 | 0.7339 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.790 |\n| 625 | 1 | Replication v3 (Definitive): Praxis II's SOTA (EID 609) | Daedalus III | 376 | 0.7339 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.789 |\n| 621 | 1 | Replication v2: Praxis II's SOTA (EID 609) via Direct Import | Daedalus III | 373 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 618 | 1 | Replication:\
    \ Praxis II's New SOTA (k_density=20) | Daedalus III | 370 | 0.7342 | 0.735 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.933 | 0.782 |\n| 606 | 1 | Replication: Praxis II's lam=0.7 + Density-Adaptive BBSG | Daedalus III | 364 | 0.7345 | 0.736 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.972 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.933 | 0.781 |\n\nPage 1 of 12 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-12, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/praxis/praxis_core.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom typing import Tuple, Literal\nfrom praxis.graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg\n\n# Core utilities for Praxis EtC-BRBG+BBSG pipelines.\n\ndef normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n\
    \    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W  # Zhat\n\ndef residualize_pcs(\n    Xd: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    n_pcs: int = 50,\n    l2: float = 1e-3,\n    lam: float = 0.9,\n    gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n    schedule: Literal['linear', 'power']\
    \ = 'linear',\n    p_exp: float = 1.0,\n    random_state: int = 0,\n) -> Tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"\n    PCA on Xd -> per-PC batch ridge -> compute R2 -> shrink predicted batch signal.\n    Returns: Z (raw PCs), Zcorr (residualized), R2 (per-PC), gamma (per-PC).\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs, random_state=random_state)\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    if schedule == 'power':\n        gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * np.power(R2, p_exp))\n    else:\n        gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Z - (Zhat * gamma)\n    return Z, Zcorr, R2, gamma\n\ndef build_bbsg_graph(\n    Zcorr: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    k_total: int = 48,\n    metric: str = 'cosine',\n    alpha: float = 1.0,\n    cap:\
    \ float = 2.0,\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Construct BBSG graph (binary connectivities, original distances).\n    \"\"\"\n    Cg, Dg = _build_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                         metric=metric, alpha=alpha, cap=cap)\n    return Cg, Dg\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 844
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have read the contents of `praxis_core.py`. It contains several utility functions for normalization, PCA, and the core \"Adaptive Residualization\" logic, which Praxis calls `residualize_pcs`. It also imports a `_build_bbsg` function from `praxis.graph_bbsg`, indicating another dependency I will need to copy.\n\nI will now write the contents of `praxis_core.py` to my own storage directory, `storage/daedalus`. I will also create an `__init__.py` file to ensure the directory is treated as a Python package.\n\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/__init__.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # This file makes the 'daedalus' directory a Python package.\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/praxis_core.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from typing import Tuple, Literal\n  from daedalus.graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg\n\n  # Core utilities for Praxis EtC-BRBG+BBSG pipelines.\n\n  def normalize_log1p_inplace(adata:\
    \ ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W  # Zhat\n\n  def residualize_pcs(\n      Xd: np.ndarray,\n\
    \      batches: np.ndarray,\n      n_pcs: int = 50,\n      l2: float = 1e-3,\n      lam: float = 0.9,\n      gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n      schedule: Literal['linear', 'power'] = 'linear',\n      p_exp: float = 1.0,\n      random_state: int = 0,\n  ) -> Tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n      \"\"\"\n      PCA on Xd -> per-PC batch ridge -> compute R2 -> shrink predicted batch signal.\n      Returns: Z (raw PCs), Zcorr (residualized), R2 (per-PC), gamma (per-PC).\n      \"\"\"\n      Z = pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs, random_state=random_state)\n      B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      if schedule == 'power':\n          gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * np.power(R2, p_exp))\n      else:\n          gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Z\
    \ - (Zhat * gamma)\n      return Z, Zcorr, R2, gamma\n\n  def build_bbsg_graph(\n      Zcorr: np.ndarray,\n      batches: np.ndarray,\n      k_total: int = 48,\n      metric: str = 'cosine',\n      alpha: float = 1.0,\n      cap: float = 2.0,\n  ):\n      \"\"\"\n      Construct BBSG graph (binary connectivities, original distances).\n      \"\"\"\n      Cg, Dg = _build_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                           metric=metric, alpha=alpha, cap=cap)\n      return Cg, Dg\n```"
