tick: 853
role: model
parts:
- text: "My first ablation study is now queued for evaluation. While awaiting the results, I will continue my methodical deconstruction of the SOTA model by preparing my second experiment.\n\nThe second key innovation in the Praxis SOTA is the Density-Adaptive Graph (DAQB). My lineage's best method used a simpler Batch-Balanced Sinkhorn Graph (BBSG). To isolate the impact of DAQB, I will replace the `build_density_adaptive_bbsg` function call with a simpler graph construction method.\n\nLooking at the `praxis_core.py` file I copied, there is a function `build_bbsg_graph` which appears to wrap the `_build_bbsg` function from `graph_bbsg.py`. This seems like the perfect candidate for a simpler, non-adaptive graph construction method to substitute into the main pipeline.\n\nI will now create a new experimental script that replaces the DAQB call with this simpler BBSG call. This will form my second ablation study.\n\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/ablation_no_daqb.py}\n```yaml\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\n  from praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict, build_bbsg_graph\n\n  def _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n      w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n      return Xd * w\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Ablation study: Replaces the Density-Adaptive (DAQB) graph with a simpler\n      Batch-Balanced Sinkhorn Graph (BBSG).\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"[daedalus_ablation_no_daqb] Using simpler BBSG graph.\")\n      \n      # Define SOTA parameters\n      alpha_emb = 0.5\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      emb_n_neighbors = 15\n      alpha_g = 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n\
    \      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam_override = 0.605\n      k_total = 50\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      cap = 2.0\n      \n      # Standard pipeline steps from SOTA\n      normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      # Embedding Path\n      Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata,\
    \ use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph Path\n      Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n      Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      lam = float(lam_override)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      # ABLATION: Use simpler BBSG instead of Density-Adaptive BBSG\n      Cg, Dg = build_bbsg_graph(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                     k_total=k_total, metric=metric, cap=cap)\n      \n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      \n      return adata\n```"
