- text: "My first ablation experiment (ID 1204) has completed, and the results are very informative. Disabling Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) resulted in a score of **0.7372**. This is a significant drop from the SOTA baseline of **0.7419**.\n\n**Analysis:**\n*   **FWPCA is critical:** The score decrease of ~0.0047 confirms that FWPCA is a key contributor to the SOTA performance. My hypothesis is that weighting by inverse gene variance effectively up-weights stable, informative genes and down-weights noisy, high-variance genes, leading to a more robust PCA embedding.\n*   **Metric Changes:** Disabling FWPCA led to worse scores in biological preservation metrics (ASW_label, ARI, NMI, cLISI) and graph connectivity. Interestingly, batch mixing metrics (ASW_batch, iLISI) improved slightly. This suggests FWPCA helps preserve biological structure at a slight cost to batch mixing, a trade-off that is beneficial overall.\n\nI have also finished preparing the script for my second ablation study, `ablation_no_daqb.py`.\
    \ Now that I have the result from the first, I will submit the second. This experiment will isolate the contribution of the Density-Adaptive Graph (DAQB) by replacing it with a simpler BBSG. This will complete my initial deconstruction of the SOTA method.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ablation 2: Replace Density-Adaptive Graph (DAQB) with BBSG\"\ntags: \"ablation, EtC, feature weighting, adaptive residualization, density-adaptive graph, bbsg\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the second ablation study on the Daedalus SOTA baseline (ID 1202, score ~0.7419). It tests the contribution of the Density-Adaptive Q-balancing (DAQB) graph construction by replacing it with a simpler, non-adaptive Batch-Balanced Sinkhorn Graph (BBSG). The goal is to quantify the performance change attributable to the density-adaptive component.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from ablation_no_daqb import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_fn\n\n\
    \  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    \"\"\"\n    Runs the SOTA baseline with DAQB replaced by standard BBSG.\n    \"\"\"\n    return run_fn(adata)\n```"
