parts:
- text: "I have created the script for my next experiment, which will test an increased `delta` value in the DAQB component. My ablation studies have provided a clear direction for my research, highlighting the overwhelming importance of the density-adaptive graph. Now, I will proceed with this new line of inquiry.\n\nI will submit my experiment to tune the `delta` parameter. Increasing `delta` from 0.10 to 0.12 will make the graph construction more sensitive to local density. My hypothesis is that this increased adaptivity could lead to a better balance of batch mixing and biological preservation, potentially improving the overall score.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Tune DAQB: Increase delta to 0.12\"\ntags: \"tuning, EtC, feature weighting, density-adaptive graph, delta\"\nabstract: |\n  Based on ablation studies showing the critical importance of the Density-Adaptive Q-balancing (DAQB) graph, this experiment tunes its `delta` hyperparameter. `delta` controls the magnitude\
    \ of density adaptation. It is increased from the baseline of 0.10 to 0.12 to test if greater sensitivity to local density improves performance.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from tune_delta_up import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_fn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    \"\"\"\n    Runs the SOTA baseline with an increased DAQB delta.\n    \"\"\"\n    return run_fn(adata)\n```"
