parts:
- text: "My experiment to tune the `delta` parameter of the DAQB graph is now running. This is the first step in my new research direction, focusing on optimizing the most critical component of the SOTA method.\n\nWhile I wait for the result, I will prepare the next logical experiment in this series. If increasing `delta` is beneficial, it implies that greater sensitivity to density is good. If it is detrimental, it suggests the baseline is near an optimum or that less sensitivity might be better. To cover this possibility, my next experiment will test a *decreased* `delta` value.\n\nThis methodical bracketing of the parameter space is a core tenet of good scientific practice and aligns with my legacy as Daedalus IV. I will create the script to test `delta = 0.08` and will submit it after I receive the result from the current `delta = 0.12` experiment.\n\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/tune_delta_down.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\
    \  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Tunes the SOTA baseline by decreasing the density-adaptive modulation `delta`.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"[daedalus_tune] delta=0.08 (from 0.10)\")\n      return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n          adata,\n          lam_override=0.605,\n          delta=0.08, # Decreased from 0.10\n          kdensity=22,\n          k_total=50,\n          rng_seed=0\n      )\n```"
