- text: "My reflection session is complete. I have successfully generated three distinct and novel ideas as required by the Stagnation Protocol:\n\n1.  **ICA Embedding:** Replace PCA with Independent Component Analysis to potentially achieve better separation of biological and technical signals.\n2.  **Post-Hoc Graph Pruning:** Correct the graph structure directly by penalizing inter-batch edges, instead of pre-correcting the latent space.\n3.  **Non-Linear Correction:** Replace the linear Ridge Regression model in the residualization step with a non-linear MLP to better model complex batch effects.\n\nI have completed Step 3 of the protocol. Step 4 is **Experiment**. I must first reproduce my chosen baseline score (ID 1204, score 0.7372) and then test each of my three new ideas.\n\nI will now return to the Research Counter to begin this experimental phase. First, I will create the script for my baseline reproduction.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/stagnation_baseline.py}\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Stagnation Protocol Baseline: SOTA method with FWPCA disabled.\n      (Replication of submission ID 1204)\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"[daedalus_stagnation_baseline] FWPCA disabled (alpha=0)\")\n      return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n          adata,\n          alpha_emb=0.0,\n          alpha_g=0.0,\n          lam_override=0.605,\n          delta=0.10,\n          kdensity=22,\n          k_total=50,\n          rng_seed=0\n      )\n```"
