tick: 863
role: model
parts:
- text: "My baseline reproduction for the Stagnation Protocol is now running. While I wait for the results, I will prepare the script for the first of my three new ideas: replacing PCA with Independent Component Analysis (ICA).\n\nThis involves modifying my baseline script. I will need to import `FastICA` from `sklearn.decomposition` and replace the `pca_array` function call with a new function that performs ICA. The rest of the pipeline, particularly the Adaptive Residualization and DAQB graph steps, will remain unchanged. This will ensure I am testing only the effect of the new embedding method.\n\nI will now write the script for this experiment.\n\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/idea1_ica_embedding.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.decomposition import FastICA\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\n  from praxis_core import\
    \ normalize_log1p_inplace, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  def ica_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ica = FastICA(n_components=n_comps, random_state=random_state, max_iter=800, whiten='unit-variance')\n      return ica.fit_transform(Xd)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Stagnation Protocol Idea 1: Replace PCA with ICA in the graph path.\n      FWPCA is disabled as per the baseline.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"[daedalus_stagnation_idea1] Using ICA instead of PCA for graph embedding.\")\n      \n      # Parameters from the baseline (ID 1204)\n      n_pcs_emb = 60 # Embedding path still uses PCA for now for stability\n      emb_n_neighbors = 15\n      n_comps_graph = 50 # Number of components for ICA\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam_override = 0.605\n      delta = 0.10\n\
    \      kdensity = 22\n      k_total = 50\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      \n      # Standard preprocessing\n      normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      # Embedding Path (Unchanged from baseline, uses standard PCA for stability)\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xd, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\
    \n      # Graph Path (MODIFIED: ICA instead of PCA)\n      Zg = ica_array(Xd, n_comps=n_comps_graph, random_state=0) # ICA call\n\n      # Remainder of the graph path is the same as the baseline\n      B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      lam = float(lam_override)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                           delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                           rng_seed=0)\n      \n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      \n      return adata\n```"
