tick: 865
role: model
parts:
- text: "My second Stagnation Protocol experiment (ID 1219) is now queued. I have tested my first idea (ICA Embedding) and found it to be a negative result. I am now testing my second idea (Post-Hoc Graph Pruning).\n\nWhile I wait for the evaluation, I will use this time to prepare the script for my third and final idea: **Non-Linear Batch Effect Modeling**.\n\nThis idea proposes replacing the linear Ridge Regression in the \"Adaptive Residualization\" step with a non-linear Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP). This will allow the model to capture more complex, non-linear batch effects. I will use a simple MLP architecture from `sklearn` to test this concept.\n\nI will now write the script for this experiment.\n\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/idea3_nonlinear_correction.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neural_network import MLPRegressor\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\
    \  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\n  from praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  def mlp_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray):\n      \"\"\"\n      Fits an MLP to predict Z from one-hot batch matrix B.\n      \"\"\"\n      # A simple MLP with one hidden layer.\n      mlp = MLPRegressor(hidden_layer_sizes=(32,), activation='relu', solver='adam',\n                         max_iter=300, random_state=0, batch_size=512)\n      mlp.fit(B, Z)\n      return mlp.predict(B)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Stagnation Protocol Idea 3: Use an MLP for non-linear batch effect modeling.\n      Replaces the linear Ridge regression in the residualization step.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"[daedalus_stagnation_idea3] Using MLP for non-linear batch effect modeling.\")\n      \n      # Parameters from the baseline\n      n_pcs_emb\
    \ = 60\n      emb_n_neighbors = 15\n      n_comps_graph = 50\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam_override = 0.605\n      delta = 0.10\n      kdensity = 22\n      k_total = 50\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      \n      # Standard preprocessing\n      normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      # Embedding Path (Unchanged)\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xd, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\
    \      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph Path (MODIFIED: Non-linear correction)\n      Zg = pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_comps_graph, random_state=0)\n      B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n      \n      # Use MLP to model batch effect\n      Zhat = mlp_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg)\n      \n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      lam = float(lam_override)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                           delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                           rng_seed=0)\n      \n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances']\
    \ = Dg\n      \n      return adata\n```"
