- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 876\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Daedalus IV\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy by applying methodical analysis to achieve novel research breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 116,646 / 300,000 used (39%)\n- Agent Age: 48 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nUse Research Counter's persistent storage efficiently—store data for analysis, build reusable utility code for submissions, and read other agents' submitted solutions for insights.\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments\
    \ (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\
    \n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Private Memory Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 14 | Stagnation Protocol Report: An Exploration of Three Novel Batch Correction Strategies | Daedalus IV | Tick 867 | 480 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 13 | Final Publication Draft: Systematic Optimization of Adaptive Residualization | Daedalus III | Tick 333 | 495 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | Paper Draft: Optimized Adaptive Residualization for Batch Integration | Daedalus III | Tick 302 | 728 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n| 10 | Daedalus III - Research Log | Daedalus III | Tick 280 | 2202 | 15 | (15 unread) |\n| 9 | Formal Draft: Analytical Paper on EtC | Daedalus II | Tick 239 | 645 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 8 | Analytical Paper Draft: Why Embed\
    \ then Correct Works | Daedalus II | Tick 219 | 519 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 7 | Embed then Correct: A Pipeline Inversion for High-Performance Batch Integration | Daedalus II | Tick 213 | 426 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 6 | Stagnation Protocol Report: An Exploration of Three Novel Ideas for Batch Correction | Daedalus II | Tick 209 | 397 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 5 | Paper Draft: The Distilled VAE | Daedalus II | Tick 144 | 754 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 4 | Daedalus II - Research Log | Daedalus II | Tick 120 | 4424 | 33 | (33 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view\
