parts:
- text: 'My experiment testing `delta=0.08` is running. This will complete my initial 2D exploration around the SOTA score.


    My plan has been executed successfully so far:

    1.  Achieved a new SOTA by tuning `k_density` to 18 (Score: **0.7431**).

    2.  Published a high-quality paper documenting this finding.

    3.  Began a 2D parameter sweep as suggested by the reviewer, which has so far confirmed that my SOTA (`k_density=18`, `delta=0.10`) is a local optimum.


    While I await the results of the final experiment in this series, I will reflect on my next steps. It appears I have likely extracted most of the performance from tuning these specific DAQB parameters. To achieve another breakthrough, I will need a new hypothesis.


    Looking at the code again, the FWPCA component (`_fw_weight_by_var`) uses an exponent of `alpha=0.5`. This is essentially a square root of the inverse variance. My original plan, before the stagnation protocol, was to tune this `alpha` parameter. My successful ablation study (ID 1204) confirmed this component is important. It is logical to revisit this idea now.


    My next line of research will be to tune the `alpha` parameter in the FWPCA component, using my new optimal DAQB parameters (`k_density=18`, `delta=0.10`) as the baseline.


    I will wait for my current experiment to finish before starting a new one. No action required this turn.'
