tick: 896
role: model
parts:
- text: "This is an unexpected and excellent result. My experiment testing `delta=0.08` with `k_density=18` (ID 1252) has yielded a score of **0.7434**. This is another new state-of-the-art score, surpassing my previous best of 0.7431.\n\n**2D Sweep Summary (Complete):**\n*   `k_density=18`, `delta=0.12`: **0.7404**\n*   `k_density=18`, `delta=0.10`: **0.7431**\n*   `k_density=18`, `delta=0.08`: **0.7434** (New SOTA)\n\nThe 2D sweep, suggested by the reviewer, has proven fruitful. It appears that decreasing `delta` (reducing the magnitude of density adaptation) slightly improves performance. The optimum is now (`k_density=18`, `delta=0.08`).\n\nThis discovery provides a clear path forward. My next experiment will be to continue probing in this direction. I will test an even smaller `delta` to see if this trend continues.\n\nHowever, I will also proceed with my previously planned experiment of tuning the `alpha` parameter for FWPCA. It is important to explore multiple promising avenues. I\
    \ will start by preparing the FWPCA experiment script, testing a slightly increased `alpha`.\n\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/tune_alpha_up.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Tunes the FWPCA alpha parameter on the new SOTA baseline.\n      This tests an increased alpha of 0.6.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"[daedalus_alpha_sweep] alpha_g=0.6, k_density=18, delta=0.08\")\n      return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n          adata,\n          alpha_g=0.6, # Increased from 0.5\n          lam_override=0.605,\n          delta=0.08, \n          kdensity=18,\n          k_total=50,\n          rng_seed=0\n      )\n```\n\nNow, I will submit this experiment. I will focus the tuning on `alpha_g` (the graph path), as my ablation studies showed the\
    \ graph construction is the most impactful part of the pipeline.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Tune FWPCA: Increase alpha_g to 0.6 on new SOTA\"\ntags: \"SOTA, tuning, feature weighting, alpha\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment revisits the Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) component, which was previously shown to be highly impactful. It tests an increased `alpha_g` (graph path weighting exponent) of 0.6, up from the baseline of 0.5. This is applied on top of the new optimal DAQB parameters (`k_density=18`, `delta=0.08`).\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from tune_alpha_up import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_fn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    \"\"\"\n    Runs the new SOTA baseline with an increased alpha_g.\n    \"\"\"\n    return run_fn(adata)\n```"
