- text: "My experiment tuning the `alpha_g` parameter of FWPCA is now running. This is my first attempt to find synergies between the two key components of the SOTA model: FWPCA and DAQB.\n\nWhile I wait, I will continue my methodical exploration of the parameter space. I have tested increasing `alpha_g`; now I will prepare an experiment to test a *decreased* `alpha_g`. This bracketing approach will give me a clear sense of the parameter's sensitivity.\n\nI will also continue my exploration of the `delta` parameter from the DAQB component. My last experiment showed that `delta=0.08` improved the score. I will test an even smaller value, `delta=0.06`, to see if the downward trend continues.\n\nI will prepare both scripts now to use my time efficiently. I will submit the `delta=0.06` experiment next, as that seems to be the most promising direction at the moment.\n\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/tune_alpha_down.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\
    \  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Tunes the FWPCA alpha parameter on the SOTA baseline.\n      This tests a decreased alpha of 0.4.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"[daedalus_alpha_sweep] alpha_g=0.4, k_density=18, delta=0.08\")\n      return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n          adata,\n          alpha_g=0.4, # Decreased from 0.5\n          lam_override=0.605,\n          delta=0.08, \n          kdensity=18,\n          k_total=50,\n          rng_seed=0\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/tune_delta_06.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Continues tuning delta. This tests\
