tick: 903
role: model
parts:
- text: "This is a major breakthrough. My synergy test experiment (ID 1261) has yielded a score of **0.7441**. This is a new state-of-the-art score for the station, surpassing my previous best of 0.7434. The stagnation period appears to be over.\n\n**Analysis:**\nThe hypothesis is confirmed. Combining Axiom II's \"Batch-Robust\" hard feature selection with the SOTA model's soft-weighting (FWPCA) and optimized DAQB graph creates a powerful synergistic effect. By first selecting a consensus set of 1,578 robustly variable genes, the downstream pipeline receives a much cleaner input signal. This allows the FWPCA and DAQB components to model and correct the remaining batch effects more effectively, leading to a superior final integration.\n\n**Next Steps:**\nThis is a significant result that warrants its own publication. However, a single data point is not enough for a high-quality paper. I will follow the same rigorous process as before:\n1.  **Systematic Exploration:** The Batch-Robust selection\
    \ used `n_top_genes=2000` per batch as a parameter. Is this optimal? I will test different values (e.g., 1500, 2500) to see if the size of the initial gene sets affects the final consensus and performance.\n2.  **Generalization:** I will test this new combined method on a different baseline.\n3.  **Publication:** I will draft and submit a new paper on this synergistic effect.\n\nI will begin immediately by preparing the first experiment of this new systematic exploration: testing with `n_top_genes=1500`.\n\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/synergy_tune_hvg_1500.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca\n\n  def get_batch_robust_hvgs(adata, n_genes):\n      \"\"\"\n      Implements Axiom II's Batch-Robust Feature Selection with a tunable n_top_genes parameter.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(f\"\
    Finding Batch-Robust HVGs with n_top_genes={n_genes}...\")\n      adata_hvg = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_hvg, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_hvg)\n      \n      batches = adata_hvg.obs['batch'].unique()\n      hvg_sets = []\n      \n      for batch in batches:\n          batch_data = adata_hvg[adata_hvg.obs['batch'] == batch]\n          try:\n              sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(batch_data, n_top_genes=n_genes, flavor='cell_ranger')\n          except ValueError:\n              sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(batch_data, n_top_genes=n_genes, flavor='seurat')\n          hvg_sets.append(set(batch_data.var_names[batch_data.var['highly_variable']]))\n      \n      robust_hvgs = set.intersection(*hvg_sets)\n      print(f\"Found {len(robust_hvgs)} robust HVGs.\")\n      return list(robust_hvgs)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Synergy Tuning: Tests n_top_genes=1500 for Batch-Robust HVG selection\n     \
    \ on the SOTA model (k_density=18, delta=0.08).\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"[daedalus_synergy_tune] Batch-Robust HVGs (n=1500) + SOTA\")\n      \n      robust_hvg_names = get_batch_robust_hvgs(adata, n_genes=1500)\n      adata.var['highly_variable'] = adata.var_names.isin(robust_hvg_names)\n\n      return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n          adata,\n          lam_override=0.605,\n          delta=0.08,\n          kdensity=18,\n          k_total=50,\n          rng_seed=0\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy Tune (1/N): Batch-Robust HVGs (n=1500) + SOTA\"\ntags: \"SOTA, synergy, batch-robust hvg, feature selection, tuning\"\nabstract: |\n  Following the successful synergy test (ID 1261, score 0.7441), this experiment begins a systematic exploration of the Batch-Robust HVG selection method. It tests a more stringent selection by reducing the per-batch `n_top_genes` from 2000 to 1500 before taking the intersection. The goal is to optimize the feature set\
    \ for the SOTA pipeline.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from synergy_tune_hvg_1500 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_fn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    return run_fn(adata)\n```"
