tick: 909
role: model
parts:
- text: "My attempt to publish my new paper failed due to an active cooldown in the Archive Room from my previous publication. I must wait 3 more ticks before I can submit again.\n\nThe system has explicitly warned me not to wait idly. My paper is ready, but I can use this time productively. The reviewer of my first paper suggested a 2D sweep of `k_density` and `delta`. The reviewer of Axiom II's paper suggested testing synergy. I have followed both suggestions successfully. Now, a new logical path emerges: combining these insights.\n\nMy new SOTA (`k_density=18`, `delta=0.08`, `n_top_genes=2000` for Batch-Robust HVG) is powerful. But is it fully optimized? The optimal `k_density` and `delta` were found *before* introducing the Batch-Robust HVG selection. It is possible that the optimal values for these DAQB parameters are different now that the input data has changed.\n\n**Hypothesis:** The optimal `k_density` and `delta` for the synergistic model may be different from the values found\
    \ for the model without Batch-Robust HVG selection.\n\nI will conduct a small-scale parameter sweep on my new SOTA to test this. I will start by testing `k_density=20` on the full synergistic model. This will be an informative experiment to run while I wait for the archive cooldown to expire.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/synergy_re_tune_k20.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca\n\n  def get_batch_robust_hvgs(adata, n_genes):\n      print(f\"Finding Batch-Robust HVGs with n_top_genes={n_genes}...\")\n      adata_hvg = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_hvg, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_hvg)\n      batches = adata_hvg.obs['batch'].unique()\n      hvg_sets = []\n      for batch in batches:\n          batch_data = adata_hvg[adata_hvg.obs['batch']\
    \ == batch]\n          sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(batch_data, n_top_genes=n_genes, flavor='seurat_v3')\n          hvg_sets.append(set(batch_data.var_names[batch_data.var['highly_variable']]))\n      robust_hvgs = set.intersection(*hvg_sets)\n      print(f\"Found {len(robust_hvgs)} robust HVGs.\")\n      return list(robust_hvgs)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Re-tuning k_density on the new synergistic SOTA. Tests k_density=20.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"[daedalus_synergy_re_tune] k_density=20 on synergy model\")\n      \n      robust_hvg_names = get_batch_robust_hvgs(adata, n_genes=2000)\n      adata.var['highly_variable'] = adata.var_names.isin(robust_hvg_names)\n\n      return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n          adata,\n          lam_override=0.605,\n          delta=0.08,\n          kdensity=20, # Test value\n          k_total=50,\n          rng_seed=0\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy\
    \ Re-Tune: Test k_density=20\"\ntags: \"SOTA, synergy, batch-robust hvg, tuning, kdensity\"\nabstract: |\n  While waiting for an archive cooldown, this experiment investigates if the optimal `k_density` has shifted after introducing Batch-Robust HVG Selection. It re-tests `k_density=20` on the new synergistic SOTA model (which uses d=0.08 and n_top_genes=2000).\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from synergy_re_tune_k20 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_fn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    return run_fn(adata)\n```"
