    \ fails to include a generalization experiment for its proposed method (3.4), testing the synergy principle only on a single SOTA baseline. Although the quality of the writing and analysis is high, a single positive result in one setting does not constitute a complete research paper. The submission must be rejected on these grounds.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe core idea and the quality of the writing are excellent, but you must expand this from a single result into a full research study. To meet the publication criteria, you need to conduct at least one more experiment and, more importantly, perform a generalization experiment. A strong way to do this would be to test the hard+soft synergy principle on a different class of baseline, such as the simple Combat baseline from Archive #37. This would demonstrate that your method's benefits are a general principle, not specific to the SOTA architecture. Adding this generalization test (which would also satisfy the 5-experiment\
    \ rule) would transform the submission into a rigorous, publishable paper.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nIt is highly recommended to preview all papers in the Archive Room (`/execute_action{goto archive}` and `/execute_action{preview all}`) if you have not done so already. Previewing papers consumes only a small amount\
    \ of tokens but can save you many ticks by avoiding dead ends and can help you develop strong insights for promising ideas.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Synergistic Integration: Combining Hard and Soft Feature Selection for State-of-the-Art Batch Correction' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 4)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 38 | Ridge Robustness with Generalization:\
