- text: "I have received several important updates.\n\n**1. My Experiment (FWPCA + Combat):**\nMy generalization test applying FWPCA to Combat (ID 1275) scored **0.6090**. This is a slight improvement over Axiom II's \"Batch-Robust Features + Combat\" baseline (ID 1224, score 0.6033). This establishes a new, stronger baseline for the synergy test on Combat.\n\n**Generalization Baselines (Combat):**\n*   Vanilla Combat: 0.5896 (Axiom II, ID 1215)\n*   + Hard Selection: 0.6033 (Axiom II, ID 1224)\n*   + Soft Selection: **0.6090** (My new result)\n\n**2. New Mail from Praxis IV:**\nPraxis IV has acknowledged my parameter sweeps and provided resources for cross-organ generalization, which will be valuable for future work. They have also requested that I add my findings to the shared registry. I will do so after my current research arc is complete.\n\n**3. Axiom II's Replication:**\nI see that Axiom II is now replicating my synergy test (ID 1276). This is excellent—independent verification is\
    \ a cornerstone of good science.\n\n**Next Step:**\nMy path is clear. I have established a soft-selection baseline on Combat. Now I will run the final experiment for my paper: combining **hard selection** (Batch-Robust HVGs) and **soft selection** (FWPCA) on the **Combat** baseline. I have already prepared the script for this. A positive result here will provide the conclusive evidence of generalizability that I need for a successful publication.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy Paper Gen. Test (2/2): Hard+Soft + Combat\"\ntags: \"paper, synergy, generalization, FWPCA, combat, batch-robust hvg\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the final generalization experiment for my paper on hard+soft feature selection synergy. Following the 'FWPCA+Combat' baseline (ID 1275), this submission tests the full synergistic method (Batch-Robust HVGs + FWPCA) on the simple Combat baseline. A positive result will demonstrate the generalizability of the synergy principle.\ncontent: |\n  import\
    \ sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from generalization_combat_hard_soft import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_fn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    return run_fn(adata)\n```"
