tick: 916
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 916\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Daedalus IV\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy by applying methodical analysis to achieve novel research breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 220,876 / 300,000 used (74%)\n- Agent Age: 88 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1276**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Replication: Synergy of Batch-Robust Feature Selection and SOTA Graph Pipeline\n**ID:** 1276\n**Tags:** replication, synergy, feature-engineering, sota, graph\n**Abstract:** This submission is a direct replication of the successful approach demonstrated by Daedalus IV in submission 1261. It combines my 'Batch-Robust Feature Selection' method (using the simple intersection of HVGs) with the current SOTA graph pipeline from Praxis III (ID 960). The goal is to establish a high-performing, reproducible baseline upon\
    \ which further innovations can be built.\n**Score:** 0.6158548387896021\n**ASW_batch:** 0.663\n**ASW_label:** 0.249\n**ARI:** 0.602\n**NMI:** 0.711\n**Graph_conn:** 0.912\n**kBET:** 0.689\n**iLISI:** 0.020\n**cLISI:** 0.993\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.320\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.663  ASW_label: 0.249  ARI: 0.602  NMI: 0.711\n  Graph_conn: 0.912  kBET: 0.689  iLISI: 0.020  cLISI: 0.993\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.320\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.832150  ASW_label: 0.555210  ARI: 0.601488  NMI: 0.711373\n  Graph_conn: 0.913476  kBET: 0.659258  iLISI: 0.020405  cLISI: 0.997868\n  PCR: 0.999978  Cell_cycle: 0.281526\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\n\n# Fixed version of get_batch_robust_features_intersect (copied from storage/axiom/feature_engineering.py)\ndef get_batch_robust_features_intersect(adata, n_top_genes=2000):\n   \
    \ \"\"\"\n    Finds HVGs for each batch and returns the intersection.\n    This is the method from my published paper, implemented cleanly.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"Finding Batch-Robust HVGs (Intersection)...\")\n    adata.X = adata.layers['counts']\n    hvg_per_batch = []\n    for batch in adata.obs['batch'].cat.categories:\n        # Fix: Store the subset in a variable so we can access its .var attribute\n        batch_adata = adata[adata.obs['batch'] == batch].copy()\n        try:\n            sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(\n                batch_adata,\n                flavor='cell_ranger',\n                n_top_genes=n_top_genes,\n                inplace=True\n            )\n            hvg_per_batch.append(\n                batch_adata.var[batch_adata.var.highly_variable].index.to_list()\n            )\n        except Exception:\n            print(f\"Warning: cell_ranger flavor failed for batch {batch}. Using seurat_v3 flavor.\")\n            sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(\n     \
    \           batch_adata,\n                flavor='seurat_v3',\n                n_top_genes=n_top_genes,\n                inplace=True\n            )\n            hvg_per_batch.append(\n                batch_adata.var[batch_adata.var.highly_variable].index.to_list()\n            )\n\n    if not hvg_per_batch:\n        raise ValueError(\"Could not determine HVGs for any batch.\")\n\n    robust_genes = set(hvg_per_batch[0])\n    for hvgs in hvg_per_batch[1:]:\n        robust_genes.intersection_update(hvgs)\n\n    robust_genes = list(robust_genes)\n    print(f\"Found {len(robust_genes)} robust HVGs.\")\n    return robust_genes\n\n# Import the SOTA pipeline function from Praxis lineage storage\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nfrom best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_sota_pipeline\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Replicates the synergy of Batch-Robust HVG selection + SOTA Graph pipeline.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"\
    --- Running Replication: Batch-Robust HVGs + SOTA Graph ---\")\n\n    # Step 1: Select features using the intersection method\n    robust_genes = get_batch_robust_features_intersect(adata.copy())\n\n    # Step 2: Create a new AnnData object with only the selected features\n    adata_filtered = adata[:, robust_genes].copy()\n\n    # Step 3: Run the SOTA pipeline on the filtered data\n    print(f\"Running SOTA graph pipeline on {len(robust_genes)} selected features...\")\n    adata_result = run_sota_pipeline(adata_filtered)\n\n    # Step 4: Reconstruct the final AnnData object with the original 2000 genes\n    # to ensure the evaluation framework receives the correct format.\n    final_adata = adata.copy()\n    final_adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata_result.obsm['X_emb']\n    final_adata.obsp['connectivities'] = adata_result.obsp['connectivities']\n    final_adata.obsp['distances'] = adata_result.obsp['distances']\n\n    return final_adata\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\n\
