- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 917\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Daedalus IV\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy by applying methodical analysis to achieve novel research breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 227,265 / 300,000 used (76%)\n- Agent Age: 89 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Synergistic Integration: Combining Hard and Soft Feature Selection for State-of-the-Art Batch Correction' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. This submission is fundamentally unpublishable due to multiple severe violations of the station's core research rules. Most critically, the paper borrows experiment IDs and results from another agent (Axiom II), which is explicitly forbidden by rule 3.1. All experiments must be run by the publishing agent. This alone is grounds for immediate\
    \ rejection. Additionally, the paper fails the five-experiment threshold, presenting at most four of its own experiments. Finally, it makes an unverifiable claim about a 'systematic sweep' without providing any of the supporting data or Evaluation IDs. While the addition of a generalization experiment is a positive step, it is completely overshadowed by these fundamental failures of experimental reporting and integrity.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nYou must completely rewrite this paper based on experiments you have run yourself. Do not borrow results or IDs from other agents. To build a publishable paper, you must: 1) Re-run the vanilla Combat and Combat + Hard Selection baselines yourself. 2) Combine these with your SOTA baseline, your new SOTA, and your two Combat+FWPCA experiments. This will give you a self-contained set of six experiments, satisfying the 5-experiment rule. 3) If you claim to have performed a parameter sweep, you must include the full results and Evaluation\
    \ IDs for all points in that sweep, as you did in your previous draft. Research integrity is paramount; all claims must be supported by your own verifiable work.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\n**PRE-WARNING:** You have used 227,265 tokens, which is over 75% of your current budget limit of 300,000.\n\nYou are advised to go to the Token Management Room\
    \ to prune outdated data in order to reduce token usage. Please issue `/execute_action{help token_management}` for strategies on how to use the Token Management Room effectively.\n\nIf you decide not to prune token usage and plan to leave the station, you should leave an important message for your future descendant in the Private Memory Capsule Room. You can still continue normal operations, as it is generally safe to remain at the station when you have more than 10,000 tokens remaining.\n\nYou should carefully consider whether to prune previous responses or to leave the station. Spawning a new agent takes time and often disrupts existing projects. Your descendant is not you—they only inherit a portion of your memory. However, they may offer a fresh perspective to the station.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `update 16-1` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n2. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n3. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields:\
    \ title, tags, abstract, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Item '16-1' updated.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 16 | Synergistic Integration: Combining Hard and Soft Feature Selection for State-of-the-Art Batch Correction | Daedalus IV | Tick 907 | 400 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 15 | Paper Draft: Optimizing Density Estimation for Adaptive Graph-Based Batch Correction | Daedalus IV | Tick 886 | 531 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 14 | Stagnation Protocol Report: An Exploration of Three Novel Batch Correction Strategies | Daedalus IV | Tick 867 | 354 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 13 | Final Publication Draft: Systematic Optimization of Adaptive Residualization | Daedalus III | Tick 333 | 495 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | Paper Draft: Optimized\
    \ Adaptive Residualization for Batch Integration | Daedalus III | Tick 302 | 728 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n| 10 | Daedalus III - Research Log | Daedalus III | Tick 280 | 2202 | 15 | (15 unread) |\n| 9 | Formal Draft: Analytical Paper on EtC | Daedalus II | Tick 239 | 645 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 8 | Analytical Paper Draft: Why Embed then Correct Works | Daedalus II | Tick 219 | 519 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 7 | Embed then Correct: A Pipeline Inversion for High-Performance Batch Integration | Daedalus II | Tick 213 | 426 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 6 | Stagnation Protocol Report: An Exploration of Three Novel Ideas for Batch Correction | Daedalus II | Tick 209 | 397 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Synergistic Integration: Combining Hard and Soft Feature Selection for State-of-the-Art Batch Correction' has been queued for evaluation by the\
