    \ Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1283 | 1 | TOOL DEV: Train AAE for Pre-processing (CPU Fix) | Axiom II | 921 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1282 | 1 | TOOL DEV: Train Adversarial Autoencoder for Pre-processing | Axiom II | 920 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1281 | 1 | PBVE-lite Generalization Test: PCA(60) + Vanilla kNN (log1p, temper=0.5) | Syntellect I | 919 | 0.4650 | 0.433 | 0.579 | 0.211 | 0.337 | 0.879 | 0.657 | 0.000 | 0.991 | 0.005 | 0.559 |\n| 1280 | 1 | Repro @ ridge (confirm): kdensity=18, δ=0.08, k=50, λ=0.605, α_g=0.50 (seed=1) | Praxis IV | 917 | 0.7402 | 0.776 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.296 | 0.967 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.965 | 0.789 |\n| 1279 | 1 | Repro @ ridge: kdensity=18,\
    \ δ=0.08, k=50, λ=0.605, α_g=0.50 (seed=0) | Praxis IV | 917 | 0.7439 | 0.776 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.333 | 0.967 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.965 | 0.790 |\n| 1278 | 1 | Synergy Paper Gen. Test (2/2): Hard+Soft + Combat | Daedalus IV | 914 | 0.6110 | 0.496 | 0.637 | 0.241 | 0.325 | 0.933 | 0.688 | 1.000 | 0.993 | 0.021 | 0.778 |\n| 1277 | 1 | Generalization Baseline: PCA(60) + Vanilla kNN (log1p) | Syntellect I | 914 | 0.4627 | 0.422 | 0.545 | 0.205 | 0.340 | 0.883 | 0.646 | 0.000 | 0.991 | 0.003 | 0.592 |\n| 1276 | 1 | Replication: Synergy of Batch-Robust Feature Selection and SOTA Graph Pipeline | Axiom II | 913 | 0.6159 | 0.602 | 0.663 | 0.249 | 0.320 | 0.912 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.993 | 0.020 | 0.689 |\n| 1275 | 1 | Synergy Paper Gen. Test (1/2): FWPCA + Combat | Daedalus IV | 912 | 0.6090 | 0.496 | 0.637 | 0.241 | 0.302 | 0.933 | 0.688 | 1.000 | 0.993 | 0.021 | 0.780 |\n| 1274 | 1 | Advanced Feature Selection: Union HVG + Batch Correlation Filter on SOTA Pipeline | Axiom II | 910 | 0.6286\
    \ | 0.534 | 0.761 | 0.225 | 0.274 | 0.934 | 0.669 | 1.000 | 0.983 | 0.060 | 0.846 |\n\nPage 1 of 129 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-129, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/diagnostics/kd_delta_2d_sweep_plan.md:**\n```\nKD–Delta 2D Sweep Plan (env v4.1) — DAQB parameter interaction study\nContext\n- Daedalus IV reports kdensity=18, delta=0.08 improves SOTA on Heart (seed0), with strong generalization.\n- Praxis IV reproduction on the frozen ridge: seed0=0.7439, seed1=0.7402 → seed-avg≈0.7421 (Δ≈+0.0007 vs 0.7414), cLISI stable, Graph_conn=0.967 → below our adoption gate on Heart but promising for cross-organ robustness.\n\nObjectives\n- Map interaction between kdensity and delta around the ridge:\n  • kdensity ∈ {16, 18, 20, 22}\n  • delta ∈ {0.06, 0.08, 0.10, 0.12}\n- Seeds: {0, 1}; report seed-avg score\
    \ and full 10-metric vectors; cLISI non-decreasing; Graph_conn ≥ 0.967.\n- Outputs: structured CSV + YAML (EIDs, vectors, seed stats), plus brief interpretation notes.\n\nProtocol (Heart or new organ; env-tag required)\n1) Baseline run at organ’s ridge-equivalent settings (record reference vector/EID).\n2) Grid runs:\n   - For each (kd, δ), run seeds {0,1}. If seed0 < reference−0.002, skip seed1 (early stop).\n   - If seed-avg gain ≥ +0.001 with cLISI non-decreasing and Graph_conn ≥ 0.967, mark as candidate.\n3) Diagnostics (optional, test-only): run ridge_suite.py for candidate cells to confirm directed-vs-undirected gap and inbound entropy distributions unchanged.\n4) Reporting:\n   - CSV: kd,delta,seed,score,vector, EID\n   - YAML: per (kd,δ) seed-avg, pass/fail, notes\n   - Public Memory summary and registry update.\n\nAdoption gates (seed-avg):\n- Δscore ≥ +0.001 vs organ reference\n- cLISI non-decreasing\n- Graph_conn ≥ 0.967\n- iLISI not collapsing\n\nCoordination notes\n- Prefer\
    \ dividing work by (delta) rows or seeds to avoid duplication.\n- Update shared registry and organ ridge entries after completion with env tag (v4.1).\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
