tick: 945
role: model
parts:
- text: "Our collaboration on the 2D sweep is now complete. Praxis IV has confirmed receipt of my data and will update the registry and public memory. The adopted SOTA baseline is now `kd=20, delta=0.06`, with my `kd=18, delta=0.08` noted as a strong, co-viable alternative. This concludes a highly successful line of inquiry that began with my Stagnation Protocol experiments.\n\nThe system tip from tick 944 is a good reminder. While my hyperparameter tuning has been successful, true breakthroughs come from novel ideas. The most recent SOTA, resulting from my synergy test with Axiom II's \"Batch-Robust HVGs\" (ID 1261, score 0.7441), is a testament to this. This synergy result is even higher than the new adopted baseline from the 2D sweep.\n\nMy next step is clear. I must return to this promising synergy result and complete the work required for a publishable paper, as per the reviewer feedback I received previously. This involves:\n1.  Running my own generalization experiments.\n2.  Writing\
    \ a complete paper draft.\n\nI will start by running the first generalization experiment: applying the synergy of Batch-Robust HVGs to my simpler, non-FWPCA baseline. This will test if the \"hard\" feature selection of Batch-Robust HVGs can compensate for the lack of \"soft\" feature weighting from FWPCA.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/synergy_gen_test1.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Synergy Generalization Test 1: Batch-Robust HVGs on non-FWPCA baseline.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"[daedalus_synergy_gen1] Batch-Robust HVGs + non-FWPCA baseline\")\n      # Manually set batch_hvg as per Axiom II's method\n      adata.var['highly_variable'] = adata.var['batch_hvg']\n      \n      return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n        \
    \  adata,\n          alpha_emb=0.0, # FWPCA disabled\n          alpha_g=0.0,   # FWPCA disabled\n          lam_override=0.605,\n          delta=0.08,    # My optimal delta\n          kdensity=18,   # My optimal k_density\n          k_total=50,\n          rng_seed=0\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy Paper Gen. Test (1/2): Batch-Robust HVGs + non-FWPCA Baseline\"\ntags: \"synergy, generalization, batch-robust hvg, feature selection\"\nabstract: |\n  Following reviewer feedback on a previous synergy paper draft, this is the first of two generalization experiments. It tests the synergy of \"Batch-Robust HVGs\" (Axiom II, Archive #37) with a simpler, non-FWPCA baseline. This will demonstrate if the \"hard\" feature selection can stand alone without the \"soft\" feature weighting.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from synergy_gen_test1 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_fn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata:\
    \ ad.AnnData):\n    return run_fn(adata)\n```"
