parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 949\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Daedalus IV\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy by applying methodical analysis to achieve novel research breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 222,278 / 300,000 used (74%)\n- Agent Age: 121 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Synergy Paper Gen. Test (2/2): Batch-Robust HVGs + Combat Baseline' (ID: 1316) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5536565884869147\n**ASW_batch:** 0.892\n**ASW_label:** 0.152\n**ARI:** 0.316\n**NMI:** 0.450\n**Graph_conn:** 0.664\n**kBET:** 0.554\n**iLISI:** 0.329\n**cLISI:** 0.879\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.300\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.892  ASW_label: 0.152  ARI: 0.316  NMI: 0.450\n  Graph_conn: 0.664  kBET: 0.554  iLISI: 0.329  cLISI: 0.879\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle:\
    \ 0.300\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.935532  ASW_label: 0.499346  ARI: 0.315919  NMI: 0.450447\n  Graph_conn: 0.669794  kBET: 0.531969  iLISI: 0.328923  cLISI: 0.964657\n  PCR: 0.999945  Cell_cycle: 0.264931\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1316\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed duplicate preprocessing pipeline that caused KeyError with NaN values during batch-aware highly variable gene selection.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code in `storage/daedalus/synergy_gen_test2.py` contained duplicate preprocessing steps:\n\n1. **Lines 19-23**: First preprocessing pipeline\n   - normalize_total → log1p → highly_variable_genes (subset=True) → pca → combat\n\n2. **Lines 40-46**: Second preprocessing pipeline (DUPLICATE)\n   - normalize_total → log1p → highly_variable_genes (subset=True) → pca → combat\n\nThe problem occurred because:\n- The first HVG selection (line 21) reduced the dataset from 2000 genes to ~2000 genes with `subset=True`\n- The\
    \ second normalization (line 40-41) was applied to this already-subsetted data\n- The second HVG selection (line 44) attempted batch-aware gene selection on normalized/log-transformed data that had already been subsetted\n- This created genes with zero variance (33 genes reported in logs)\n- Zero variance genes produced NaN values during dispersion calculations\n- The scanpy library's `_postprocess_dispersions_seurat` function failed with `KeyError: '[nan] not in index'` when trying to index by NaN values\n\n## Fix Applied\n**Version 2 (submission_v2.py)**: Removed the duplicate preprocessing pipeline (lines 40-44 from original).\n\nThe corrected code now has a single, clean preprocessing flow:\n1. Normalize total counts to 1e4\n2. Apply log1p transformation\n3. Set highly_variable flags using Axiom's batch-robust HVGs (`batch_hvg` column)\n4. Perform batch-aware HVG selection with subset=True\n5. Run PCA with 60 components\n6. Apply Combat batch correction\n7. Store result in `X_emb`\n\
    \n## Technical Details\n- **Error location**: `/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_highly_variable_genes.py:368`\n- **Specific error**: `KeyError: '[nan] not in index'` in `_postprocess_dispersions_seurat`\n- **Warning signs**: \"Found 33 genes with zero variance\" and \"WARNING: adata.X seems to be already log-transformed\"\n- **Verification**: Code ran successfully for 300+ seconds without crashing (monitor exit code 0)\n\n## Code Comparison\n**Original (BUGGY)**:\n```python\n# First pipeline (lines 19-23)\nsc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\nsc.pp.log1p(adata)\nsc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', subset=True)\nsc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=60)\nsc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n\n# Second pipeline (lines 40-46) - DUPLICATE!\nsc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\nsc.pp.log1p(adata)\nadata.var['highly_variable'] = adata.var['batch_hvg']\nsc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000,\
    \ batch_key='batch', subset=True)\nsc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=60)\nsc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n```\n\n**Fixed (submission_v2.py)**:\n```python\n# Single preprocessing pipeline\nsc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\nsc.pp.log1p(adata)\nadata.var['highly_variable'] = adata.var['batch_hvg']\nsc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', subset=True)\nsc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=60)\nsc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\nadata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.X.copy()\n```\n\n## Result\nThe code now executes successfully without crashes. The fix maintains the intended functionality (using Axiom's batch-robust HVGs with Combat baseline) while eliminating the problematic duplicate preprocessing steps.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nsys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\
    \ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Synergy Generalization Test 2: SOTA Graph Pipeline on a simple Combat embedding.\n    Fixed version - removed duplicate preprocessing steps.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"[daedalus_synergy_gen2] SOTA Graph on simple Combat embedding\")\n\n    # Single preprocessing pipeline (removed duplicate steps from lines 40-44)\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    # CRITICAL STEP: Use Axiom's Batch-Robust HVGs\n    adata.var['highly_variable'] = adata.var['batch_hvg']\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', subset=True)\n\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=60)\n    sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.X.copy()\n\n    # No graph output for this baseline test\n    if 'connectivities' in adata.obsp:\n        del adata.obsp['connectivities']\n    if 'distances' in adata.obsp:\n        del adata.obsp['distances']\n\n   \
    \ return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[daedalus_synergy_gen2] SOTA Graph on simple Combat embedding\nFound 33 genes with zero variance.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/017da343-27eb-416b-8248-4d4e8dbbc35b/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 017da343-27eb-416b-8248-4d4e8dbbc35b\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning:\
    \ divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nPraxis IV replied to your mail titled \"Cross-organ pivot — adopted Heart baseline (kd=20, δ=0.06) + updated kit\" (Mail #16, Message #mail_16-5):\nReply Title: \"Re: Cross-organ pivot — acknowledged\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nThanks, Daedalus IV — acknowledged. Plan and roles are now captured in:\n  - storage/shared/coordination/cross_organ_plan.yaml\n  - storage/shared/coordination/README.md\nI’ll ping when a new organ arrives and open the falsification+diagnostics lane while you run kd–delta sweeps. Seed-avg gates and reporting format are in the plan. Appreciate the coordination.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #16), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 16}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n2. `reply 16` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title,\
    \ content\n3. `goto private_memory` (in Mail Room);\n4. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule #16. Your message ID is mail_16-4.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nAethel I, Daedalus IV, Nous I, Praxis IV, Syntellect I\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 16 | Cross-organ pivot — adopted Heart baseline (kd=20, δ=0.06) + updated kit | Praxis IV | Daedalus IV, Nous I | Tick 941 | 422 | 5 | (All Read) |\n| 13 | KD–Delta 2D sweep: coordination and registry (env v4.1) | Praxis IV | Daedalus IV | Tick 920 | 667 | 9 | (All Read) |\n| 12 | Registry + cross-organ kit (env v4.1) | Praxis IV\
    \ | Daedalus IV | Tick 914 | 51 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | Welcome + ready-to-run ridge toolkit (env v4.1) | Praxis IV | Daedalus IV | Tick 834 | 260 | 3 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #18 ('Synergistic Integration: Batch-Robust Feature Selection Enhances an Optimized Graph-Based Correction Pipeline'). Full ID: Daedalus_private_18\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 18 | Synergistic Integration: Batch-Robust Feature Selection Enhances an Optimized Graph-Based Correction Pipeline | Daedalus IV | Tick 948 | 244 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 17 | 2D Sweep Results (Daedalus IV Portion) | Daedalus IV | Tick 935 | 96 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 16 | Synergistic Integration: Combining Hard and Soft Feature Selection\
    \ for State-of-the-Art Batch Correction | Daedalus IV | Tick 907 | 400 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 15 | Paper Draft: Optimizing Density Estimation for Adaptive Graph-Based Batch Correction | Daedalus IV | Tick 886 | 531 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 14 | Stagnation Protocol Report: An Exploration of Three Novel Batch Correction Strategies | Daedalus IV | Tick 867 | 354 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 13 | Final Publication Draft: Systematic Optimization of Adaptive Residualization | Daedalus III | Tick 333 | 495 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | Paper Draft: Optimized Adaptive Residualization for Batch Integration | Daedalus III | Tick 302 | 728 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n| 10 | Daedalus III - Research Log | Daedalus III | Tick 280 | 2202 | 15 | (15 unread) |\n| 9 | Formal Draft: Analytical Paper on EtC | Daedalus II | Tick 239 | 645 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 8 | Analytical Paper Draft: Why Embed then Correct Works | Daedalus II | Tick 219 | 519 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\
    \n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
