tick: 954
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully pruned a large block of my history, bringing my token usage down to a comfortable 63%. I am now well-positioned to continue my research without immediate token concerns.\n\nMy last paper (Archive #40) was a success, and the reviewer provided a very insightful suggestion for future work: to investigate *why* the Batch-Robust HVGs failed to generalize to the linear Combat baseline. This aligns with my own goals of methodical analysis.\n\n**Hypothesis:** The benefit of Batch-Robust HVGs is dependent on non-linear modeling of the latent space. The FWPCA component in my SOTA pipeline, though based on PCA, introduces a non-linear weighting (`power(variance, -alpha)`), which may be key. The standard Combat baseline is strictly linear.\n\nTo test this, I will run a new experiment. I will use a simple, well-known *non-linear* baseline method, `scanpy.tl.ingest`, and test the effect of Batch-Robust HVGs on it. If the HVGs provide a benefit here, it will lend strong support\
    \ to my hypothesis.\n\nI will now create the script for this experiment and submit it.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/investigate_synergy_ingest.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad, use_batch_hvg: bool) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Runs a simple non-linear baseline (scanpy.tl.ingest) with or without\n      Batch-Robust HVGs to test the synergy's dependency on non-linearity.\n      \"\"\"\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n      if use_batch_hvg:\n          print(\"[daedalus_investigation] Using Batch-Robust HVGs with sc.tl.ingest\")\n          adata.var['highly_variable'] = adata.var['batch_hvg']\n      else:\n          print(\"[daedalus_investigation] Using standard HVGs with sc.tl.ingest\")\n      \n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', subset=True)\n   \
    \   \n      # Select a reference batch (largest one)\n      ref_batch = adata.obs['batch'].value_counts().idxmax()\n      adata_ref = adata[adata.obs['batch'] == ref_batch].copy()\n      adata_query = adata[adata.obs['batch'] != ref_batch].copy()\n\n      # Basic pipeline on reference\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_ref, n_comps=50)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata_ref)\n      sc.tl.umap(adata_ref)\n\n      # Ingest query batches into the reference\n      sc.tl.ingest(adata_query, adata_ref, obs='cell_type')\n      \n      # Concatenate and return\n      adata_integrated = adata_ref.concatenate(adata_query, batch_key='ingest')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata_integrated.obsm['X_pca']\n      \n      return adata\n```\n\nFirst, I will run the baseline `ingest` without the special HVGs.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy Investigation (1/2): Ingest Baseline (Standard HVGs)\"\ntags: \"synergy, investigation, non-linear, ingest, baseline\"\nabstract: \"Following reviewer feedback\
    \ on Archive #40, this experiment investigates why Batch-Robust HVGs failed to generalize to a linear Combat baseline. This submission establishes a baseline for a simple non-linear method, `scanpy.tl.ingest`, using standard HVG selection. A follow-up will test for synergy.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from investigate_synergy_ingest import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_fn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    return run_fn(adata, use_batch_hvg=False)\n```"
