- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 955\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Daedalus IV\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy by applying methodical analysis to achieve novel research breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 194,350 / 300,000 used (65%)\n- Agent Age: 127 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Synergy Investigation (2/2): Ingest with Batch-Robust HVGs' (ID: 1326) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nAutoResearchEvaluator: Set memory limit to 96g\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn,\
    \ executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[daedalus_investigation] Using Batch-Robust HVGs with sc.tl.ingest\n\n\nSTDERR:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/pandas/core/indexes/base.py\", line 3812, in get_loc\n    return self._engine.get_loc(casted_key)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"pandas/_libs/index.pyx\", line 167, in pandas._libs.index.IndexEngine.get_loc\n  File \"pandas/_libs/index.pyx\", line 196, in pandas._libs.index.IndexEngine.get_loc\n  File \"pandas/_libs/hashtable_class_helper.pxi\", line 7088, in pandas._libs.hashtable.PyObjectHashTable.get_item\n  File \"pandas/_libs/hashtable_class_helper.pxi\", line 7096, in pandas._libs.hashtable.PyObjectHashTable.get_item\nKeyError: 'cell_type'\n\nThe above exception was the direct cause of the following exception:\n\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/tmp/tmpdk_6_ke3/storage/system/main.py\", line\
    \ 113, in <module>\n    main()\n  File \"/tmp/tmpdk_6_ke3/storage/system/main.py\", line 75, in main\n    adata_result = eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata_input)\n                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/tmp/tmpdk_6_ke3/submission.py\", line 7, in eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n    return run_fn(adata, use_batch_hvg=True)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/tmp/tmpdk_6_ke3/storage/daedalus/investigate_synergy_ingest.py\", line 32, in eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n    sc.tl.ingest(adata_query, adata_ref, obs='cell_type')\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/legacy_api_wrap/__init__.py\", line 82, in fn_compatible\n    return fn(*args_all, **kw)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/tools/_ingest.py\", line 153, in ingest\n    ing.map_labels(col, labeling_method[i])\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/tools/_ingest.py\"\
    , line 460, in map_labels\n    self._obs[labels] = self._knn_classify(labels)\n                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/tools/_ingest.py\", line 448, in _knn_classify\n    cat_array: pd.Series = self._adata_ref.obs[labels].astype(\"category\")\n                           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/pandas/core/frame.py\", line 4107, in __getitem__\n    indexer = self.columns.get_loc(key)\n              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/pandas/core/indexes/base.py\", line 3819, in get_loc\n    raise KeyError(key) from err\nKeyError: 'cell_type'\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Synergy Investigation (1/2): Ingest Baseline (Standard HVGs)' (ID: 1322) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.32614971309608504\n\
    **ASW_batch:** 0.936\n**ASW_label:** 0.115\n**ARI:** 0.000\n**NMI:** 0.004\n**Graph_conn:** 0.183\n**kBET:** 0.299\n**iLISI:** 0.517\n**cLISI:** 0.208\n**PCR:** 0.998\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.000\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.936  ASW_label: 0.115  ARI: 0.000  NMI: 0.004\n  Graph_conn: 0.183  kBET: 0.299  iLISI: 0.517  cLISI: 0.208\n  PCR: 0.998  Cell_cycle: 0.000\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.955239  ASW_label: 0.478176  ARI: -0.000063  NMI: 0.004153\n  Graph_conn: 0.197256  kBET: 0.292072  iLISI: 0.517416  cLISI: 0.769427\n  PCR: 0.997975  Cell_cycle: 0.005714\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1322\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the crashing code by removing an invalid parameter from the `sc.tl.ingest()` function call.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code (evaluation 1322) was attempting to use `sc.tl.ingest(adata_query, adata_ref, obs='cell_type')` on line 32 of the imported\
    \ function from `storage/daedalus/investigate_synergy_ingest.py`.\n\nThe error occurred because:\n1. The `sc.tl.ingest()` function was trying to map cell type labels from the reference dataset to the query dataset\n2. The dataset does NOT contain a 'cell_type' column in the observations\n3. The dataset only has two columns: 'batch' and 'observation_joinid'\n\nThe full error was:\n```\nKeyError: 'cell_type'\n  File \"/tmp/tmph_v9nxft/storage/daedalus/investigate_synergy_ingest.py\", line 32, in eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n    sc.tl.ingest(adata_query, adata_ref, obs='cell_type')\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the following change:\n\n**Before (buggy code in lineage file):**\n```python\nsc.tl.ingest(adata_query, adata_ref, obs='cell_type')\n```\n\n**After (fixed code in submission_v2.py):**\n```python\nsc.tl.ingest(adata_query, adata_ref)\n```\n\nThe fix involved:\n1. Copying the entire `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` function from the lineage file into\
    \ submission_v2.py\n2. Removing the `obs='cell_type'` parameter from the `sc.tl.ingest()` call on line 32\n3. Adding a comment explaining the fix\n\nThe `obs` parameter is optional in `sc.tl.ingest()`. When omitted, the function performs the ingest operation without attempting to transfer cell type annotations, which is appropriate since this dataset doesn't contain cell type labels.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that submission_v2.py is running successfully:\n- Exit code: 0 (SUCCESS)\n- No crash detected after 600.5 seconds\n- Code is executing in the evaluation system without errors\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Version**: submission_v2.py\n- **Approach**: Removed invalid parameter rather than try to add missing data\n- **Reasoning**: The sc.tl.ingest function can work without cell type labels; it will still perform the dimensional reduction and neighbor graph integration\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code\
    \ relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nsys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Runs a simple non-linear baseline (scanpy.tl.ingest) with standard HVGs\n    to test the synergy's dependency on non-linearity.\n\n    Fixed: Removed obs='cell_type' parameter from sc.tl.ingest since the dataset\n    doesn't have cell_type labels.\n    \"\"\"\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    print(\"[daedalus_investigation] Using standard HVGs with sc.tl.ingest\")\n\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', subset=True)\n\n    # Select a reference batch (largest one)\n    ref_batch = adata.obs['batch'].value_counts().idxmax()\n    adata_ref = adata[adata.obs['batch'] == ref_batch].copy()\n    adata_query = adata[adata.obs['batch']\
    \ != ref_batch].copy()\n\n    # Basic pipeline on reference\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_ref, n_comps=50)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata_ref)\n    sc.tl.umap(adata_ref)\n\n    # Ingest query batches into the reference\n    # Fixed: Removed obs='cell_type' since dataset doesn't have cell_type column\n    sc.tl.ingest(adata_query, adata_ref)\n\n    # Concatenate and return\n    adata_integrated = adata_ref.concatenate(adata_query, batch_key='ingest')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata_integrated.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[daedalus_investigation] Using standard HVGs with sc.tl.ingest\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/a856f003-1399-4b42-ac9b-2e1f25bc845e/result_human.h5ad\n\
    \nRESULT_UUID: a856f003-1399-4b42-ac9b-2e1f25bc845e\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Synergy Investigation (2/2): Ingest with Batch-Robust HVGs' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 1326.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1326 | 1\
