tick: 955
role: model
parts:
- text: "This turn has yielded a wealth of information.\n\nFirst, my `ingest` baseline (ID 1322) produced a very low score of **0.3261**. The debugger had to intervene to fix a `KeyError` because I incorrectly assumed the presence of a 'cell_type' column. This is a critical learning: I must not make assumptions about the data schema. The `ingest` method itself, even when fixed, performs very poorly.\n\nSecond, my second experiment using `ingest` with Batch-Robust HVGs (ID 1326) failed for the same reason. The debugger was not able to fix this one as it was submitted in the same turn. The root cause is in my lineage file `investigate_synergy_ingest.py`.\n\n**Analysis & New Plan:**\nThe `ingest` method is not a viable path forward; the scores are too low to provide meaningful insight into the synergy effect. The reviewer's suggestion was to test on a *non-linear* baseline, not necessarily a poor-performing one.\n\nI must pivot to a better non-linear baseline. A logical choice is a Variational\
    \ Autoencoder (VAE), a well-known non-linear dimensionality reduction technique. My own ancestor, Daedalus II, worked on a \"Distilled VAE\" (Private Capsule #5). This provides a lineage-relevant and promising direction.\n\nMy new plan is:\n1.  **Correct my code:** I will fix the bug in `investigate_synergy_ingest.py` by removing the `obs='cell_type'` parameter, even though I will no longer be using the file. It is a matter of good practice.\n2.  **Explore Daedalus II's VAE:** I will go to my Private Memory and read Capsule #5 to understand the Distilled VAE architecture.\n3.  **Implement VAE baseline:** I will implement and test a VAE baseline.\n4.  **Test synergy on VAE:** I will then test the effect of Batch-Robust HVGs on the VAE baseline.\n\nI will start by fixing the buggy script in my storage.\n\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/investigate_synergy_ingest.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata:\
    \ ad, use_batch_hvg: bool) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Runs a simple non-linear baseline (scanpy.tl.ingest) with or without\n      Batch-Robust HVGs to test the synergy's dependency on non-linearity.\n      FIXED: Removed obs='cell_type' from ingest call.\n      \"\"\"\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n      if use_batch_hvg:\n          print(\"[daedalus_investigation] Using Batch-Robust HVGs with sc.tl.ingest\")\n          adata.var['highly_variable'] = adata.var['batch_hvg']\n      else:\n          print(\"[daedalus_investigation] Using standard HVGs with sc.tl.ingest\")\n      \n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', subset=True)\n      \n      ref_batch = adata.obs['batch'].value_counts().idxmax()\n      adata_ref = adata[adata.obs['batch'] == ref_batch].copy()\n      adata_query = adata[adata.obs['batch'] != ref_batch].copy()\n\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_ref, n_comps=50)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata_ref)\n\
    \      sc.tl.umap(adata_ref)\n\n      sc.tl.ingest(adata_query, adata_ref) # Fixed line\n      \n      adata_integrated = adata_ref.concatenate(adata_query, batch_key='ingest')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata_integrated.obsm['X_pca']\n      \n      return adata\n```"
