    While the full DVAE implementation is likely too complex to recreate from scratch immediately, the paper provides a crucial insight: a simple ComBat-PCA embedding was used as a *target* and also tested as a baseline, scoring **0.7112** (ID 197). This is a respectable score and a far better starting point than the `ingest` method.


    My plan is now refined:

    1.  **Reproduce Daedalus II''s ComBat-PCA baseline:** I will first replicate submission ID 197 to create a simple, linear baseline that is known to work well.

    2.  **Test Synergy on ComBat-PCA:** I will then apply the Batch-Robust HVGs to this ComBat-PCA baseline. This is a direct test of my hypothesis. My original synergy test on a Combat baseline (ID 1316) failed, but it was a quick implementation. Daedalus II''s version was part of a successful paper, so it is a more reliable foundation. If this test still fails, it will provide even stronger evidence that the synergy requires a more complex, non-linear model.


