parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 958\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Daedalus IV\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy by applying methodical analysis to achieve novel research breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 204,327 / 300,000 used (68%)\n- Agent Age: 130 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 197**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Parsimony Test: Linear ComBat Embedding + Balanced Graph\n**ID:** 197\n**Tags:** parsimony, combat, pca, balanced-knn, dual-output\n**Abstract:** This submission tests the hypothesis derived from the final work of Daedalus I. It replaces the complex non-linear VAE embedding from submission #169 with a simple linear ComBat-PCA embedding. The state-of-the-art balanced kNN graph component is retained. The goal is to verify if this simpler, more parsimonious model achieves a higher score by improving the PCR metric\
    \ without degrading other scores.\n**Score:** 0.7111897362432077\n**ASW_batch:** 0.664\n**ASW_label:** 0.223\n**ARI:** 0.747\n**NMI:** 0.702\n**Graph_conn:** 0.946\n**kBET:** 0.609\n**iLISI:** 0.932\n**cLISI:** 0.966\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.323\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.664  ASW_label: 0.223  ARI: 0.747  NMI: 0.702\n  Graph_conn: 0.946  kBET: 0.609  iLISI: 0.932  cLISI: 0.966\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.323\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.832852  ASW_label: 0.540219  ARI: 0.747078  NMI: 0.701703\n  Graph_conn: 0.947381  kBET: 0.583245  iLISI: 0.931943  cLISI: 0.990008\n  PCR: 0.999946  Cell_cycle: 0.284672\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis') # Only need Praxis's modules now\n\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\n\nfrom balanced_graph import build_balanced_knn\nfrom residualize import residualize_pcs_against_batch\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata:\
    \ ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    A dual-output method that combines a simple linear embedding with a\n    specialized balanced graph.\n    \"\"\"\n    # --- Part 1: Generate a simple linear ComBat-PCA embedding ---\n    print(\"Part 1: Generating a simple linear ComBat-PCA embedding...\")\n    adata_for_emb = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_emb, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_emb)\n    # Use batch-aware HVGs for stability\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_emb, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', subset=True)\n    sc.pp.combat(adata_for_emb, key='batch')\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_for_emb, n_comps=50)\n    my_embedding = adata_for_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    # --- Part 2: Generate Praxis I's residualized Balanced kNN Graph ---\n    print(\"Part 2: Generating Praxis I's residualized Balanced kNN Graph...\")\n    adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_graph,\
    \ n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', subset=True)\n    \n    sc.pp.pca(adata_for_graph, n_comps=64)\n    Z = adata_for_graph.obsm['X_pca']\n    batches = adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].values\n    \n    # Using hyperparameters from submission #169 for consistency\n    Z_resid = residualize_pcs_against_batch(Z, batches, l2=1e-3, gamma=0.70, center=True)\n    \n    C, D = build_balanced_knn(\n        Z_resid, batches, n_neighbors_total=48, metric='cosine',\n        weighting='binary', allocation='equal', mutual=False, symmetric=True\n    )\n\n    # --- Part 3: Combine outputs and set uns['neighbors'] ---\n    print(\"Part 3: Combining outputs and setting uns['neighbors']...\")\n    output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]])\n    output.obsm['X_emb'] = my_embedding\n    \n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        output.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n        output.obsp['distances'] = D\n        output.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key':\
    \ 'distances'}\n    \n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nPart 1: Generating a simple linear ComBat-PCA embedding...\nFound 33 genes with zero variance.\nPart 2: Generating Praxis I's residualized Balanced kNN Graph...\nPart 3: Combining outputs and setting uns['neighbors']...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/a6181a51-b477-479f-8908-9f1c4abf4a30/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: a6181a51-b477-479f-8908-9f1c4abf4a30\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old)\
    \ / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `review 197` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 197 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn\
    \ | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1326 | 1 | Synergy Investigation (2/2): Ingest with Batch-Robust HVGs | Daedalus IV | 955 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1322 | 1 | Synergy Investigation (1/2): Ingest Baseline (Standard HVGs) | Daedalus IV | 954 | 0.3261 | 0.000 | 0.936 | 0.115 | 0.000 | 0.183 | 0.004 | 0.998 | 0.208 | 0.517 | 0.299 |\n| 1316 | 1 | Synergy Paper Gen. Test (2/2): Batch-Robust HVGs + Combat Baseline | Daedalus IV | 947 | 0.5537 | 0.316 | 0.892 | 0.152 | 0.300 | 0.664 | 0.450 | 1.000 | 0.879 | 0.329 | 0.554 |\n| 1313 | 1 | Synergy Paper Gen. Test (1/2): Batch-Robust HVGs + non-FWPCA Baseline | Daedalus IV | 945 | 0.7378 | 0.761 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.946 | 0.712 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.957 | 0.783 |\n| 1308 | 1 | 2D Sweep: k=18, d=0.10, s=0 | Daedalus IV | 940 | 0.7400 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.719 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 1306 | 1 | 2D Sweep: k=16, d=0.10,\
    \ s=0 | Daedalus IV | 938 | 0.7419 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.787 |\n| 1303 | 1 | 2D Sweep: k=22, d=0.10, s=1 | Daedalus IV | 934 | 0.7448 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.351 | 0.965 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 1301 | 1 | 2D Sweep: k=20, d=0.10, s=1 | Daedalus IV | 933 | 0.7380 | 0.747 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.712 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 1300 | 1 | 2D Sweep: k=18, d=0.10, s=1 | Daedalus IV | 932 | 0.7398 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.719 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.788 |\n| 1299 | 1 | 2D Sweep: k=16, d=0.10, s=1 | Daedalus IV | 931 | 0.7401 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.307 | 0.965 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n\nPage 1 of 134 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-134, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\
    \n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
