parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 959\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Daedalus IV\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy by applying methodical analysis to achieve novel research breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 208,004 / 300,000 used (69%)\n- Agent Age: 131 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/praxis/balanced_graph.py` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage read storage/praxis/residualize.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/praxis/balanced_graph.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for storage/praxis/residualize.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\
    \nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1326 | 1 | Synergy Investigation (2/2): Ingest with Batch-Robust HVGs | Daedalus IV | 955 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1322 | 1 | Synergy Investigation (1/2): Ingest Baseline (Standard HVGs) | Daedalus IV | 954 | 0.3261 | 0.000 | 0.936 | 0.115 | 0.000 | 0.183 | 0.004 | 0.998 | 0.208 | 0.517 | 0.299 |\n| 1316 | 1 | Synergy Paper Gen. Test (2/2): Batch-Robust HVGs + Combat Baseline | Daedalus IV | 947 | 0.5537 | 0.316 | 0.892 | 0.152 | 0.300 | 0.664 | 0.450 | 1.000 | 0.879 | 0.329 | 0.554 |\n| 1313 | 1 | Synergy Paper Gen. Test (1/2): Batch-Robust HVGs + non-FWPCA Baseline | Daedalus IV | 945 | 0.7378 | 0.761 | 0.681 | 0.218\
    \ | 0.352 | 0.946 | 0.712 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.957 | 0.783 |\n| 1308 | 1 | 2D Sweep: k=18, d=0.10, s=0 | Daedalus IV | 940 | 0.7400 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.719 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 1306 | 1 | 2D Sweep: k=16, d=0.10, s=0 | Daedalus IV | 938 | 0.7419 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.787 |\n| 1303 | 1 | 2D Sweep: k=22, d=0.10, s=1 | Daedalus IV | 934 | 0.7448 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.351 | 0.965 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 1301 | 1 | 2D Sweep: k=20, d=0.10, s=1 | Daedalus IV | 933 | 0.7380 | 0.747 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.712 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 1300 | 1 | 2D Sweep: k=18, d=0.10, s=1 | Daedalus IV | 932 | 0.7398 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.719 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.788 |\n| 1299 | 1 | 2D Sweep: k=16, d=0.10, s=1 | Daedalus IV | 931 | 0.7401 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.307 | 0.965 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n\nPage 1 of 134 (sorted\
    \ by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-134, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/praxis/balanced_graph.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom scipy.sparse import coo_matrix, csr_matrix\n\ndef build_balanced_knn(\n    Z,\n    batches,\n    n_neighbors_total=15,\n    metric='euclidean',\n    weighting='binary',      # 'binary' or 'gaussian'\n    allocation='equal',      # 'equal' or 'proportional'\n    mutual=False,            # keep edge only if i in N(j) and j in N(i)\n    symmetric=True           # symmetrize final graph\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Build a batch-balanced kNN graph over embedding Z.\n\n    Strategy:\n    - For each batch b, fit a NN index on cells from batch b.\n    - For each query cell i, retrieve k_b neighbors from batch b (dropping self if present).\n\
    \    - Aggregate across batches to approximate ~n_neighbors_total per node.\n    - If mutual=True, keep only pairs that appear in both directions (i->j and j->i).\n    - Distances are stored; connectivities are either binary or gaussian-weighted.\n\n    Parameters:\n      Z: (n, d) embedding (np array)\n      batches: (n,) array-like batch labels\n      n_neighbors_total: desired total neighbors per node after combining batches\n      metric: NN distance metric\n      weighting:\n        - 'binary': connectivities = 1.0 on edges\n        - 'gaussian': exp(-d^2/(2*s_bar^2)), s_bar from per-node median distances\n      allocation:\n        - 'equal': k_b = ceil(n_neighbors_total / B) for all batches (B = #unique batches)\n        - 'proportional': k_b ∝ batch size; k_b >= 1\n      mutual: retain only edges observed in both directions\n      symmetric: ensure C and D are symmetric\n\n    Returns:\n      C: CSR connectivities (n x n)\n      D: CSR distances (n x n)\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z,\
    \ dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    B = len(uniq)\n    if n == 0 or B == 0:\n        return None, None\n\n    # Determine per-batch neighbor quotas k_b\n    counts = {b: int((batches == b).sum()) for b in uniq}\n    if allocation == 'proportional':\n        total = float(n)\n        k_map = {}\n        # round and ensure at least 1\n        for b in uniq:\n            frac = counts[b] / total if total > 0 else 0.0\n            k_map[b] = max(1, int(round(n_neighbors_total * frac)))\n        # fallback guarantee: ensure at least 1 per batch and nonzero total\n        if sum(k_map.values()) == 0:\n            for b in uniq:\n                k_map[b] = 1\n    else:\n        base = max(1, int(np.ceil(n_neighbors_total / max(1, B))))\n        k_map = {b: base for b in uniq}\n\n    # Gather directed edges (i->j) with minimal distances\n    dir_edges = {}  # (i,j) -> dist\n\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train = np.where(batches\
    \ == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0:\n            continue\n        k_b = k_map[b]\n        k_query = min(k_b + 1, idx_train.size)  # +1 to allow self, will drop later\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_query, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n\n        # Query using all cells\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k_query, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[inds]  # map batch-local to global indices\n\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:k_b]\n            di = di[mask][:k_b]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j:\n                    continue\n                key = (int(i), int(j))\n                prev = dir_edges.get(key)\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    dir_edges[key] = float(d)\n\n    # Convert to undirected pairs with minimum distance\
    \ rule\n    pairs = {}\n    if mutual:\n        # keep only if both directions exist\n        for (i, j), d_ij in dir_edges.items():\n            if (j, i) in dir_edges:\n                d_ji = dir_edges[(j, i)]\n                d = min(d_ij, d_ji)\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs[(a, c)] = d\n    else:\n        # keep if either direction exists, using min distance if both\n        for (i, j), d_ij in dir_edges.items():\n            a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n            d = d_ij\n            if (j, i) in dir_edges:\n                d = min(d, dir_edges[(j, i)])\n            prev = pairs.get((a, c))\n            if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                pairs[(a, c)] = d\n\n    if not pairs:\n        return None, None\n\n    # Build symmetric distance matrix\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs.items():\n\
    \        rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dist_data.append(d)\n        if symmetric:\n            rows.append(j); cols.append(i); dist_data.append(d)\n\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n\n    # Connectivities\n    if weighting == 'binary':\n        C = D.copy()\n        C.data[:] = 1.0\n        return C.tocsr(), D\n    elif weighting == 'gaussian':\n        # Per-node scale: median incident distance (fallback to global median)\n        s = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n        for i in range(n):\n            start, end = D.indptr[i], D.indptr[i+1]\n            di = D.data[start:end]\n            if di.size > 0:\n                s[i] = np.median(di)\n        global_med = np.median(D.data) if D.nnz > 0 else 1.0\n        s[s <= 0] = global_med if global_med > 0 else 1.0\n\n        rows_w, cols_w, w_data = [], [], []\n        for i in range(n):\n            start, end = D.indptr[i], D.indptr[i+1]\n            js = D.indices[start:end]\n            di =\
    \ D.data[start:end]\n            if js.size == 0:\n                continue\n            s_bar = 0.5 * (s[i] + s[js])\n            denom = 2.0 * (s_bar * s_bar) + 1e-12\n            w = np.exp(- (di * di) / denom).astype(np.float32)\n            rows_w.extend([i] * len(js)); cols_w.extend(js.tolist()); w_data.extend(w.tolist())\n\n        C = coo_matrix((w_data, (rows_w, cols_w)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n        if symmetric:\n            C = C.maximum(C.transpose()).tocsr()\n        return C, D\n    else:\n        C = D.copy()\n        C.data[:] = 1.0\n        return C.tocsr(), D\n\n```\n---\n**storage/praxis/residualize.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef residualize_pcs_against_batch(Z, batches, l2=1e-3, gamma=0.2, center=True):\n    \"\"\"\n    Linear ridge residualization of PCs Z against one-hot batch indicators.\n    Z: (n, d) embedding (float32/float64)\n    batches: array-like length n (categorical)\n    l2: ridge penalty\n    gamma: fraction of predicted batch component to\
    \ subtract (0=no change, 1=full residualization)\n    center: if True, center Z globally before regression and re-add mean after residualization\n    Returns Z_resid (n, d)\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    n, d = Z.shape\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    B = np.zeros((n, len(uniq)), dtype=np.float32)\n    for k, u in enumerate(uniq):\n        B[:, k] = (batches == u).astype(np.float32)\n\n    if center:\n        mu = Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n        Zc = Z - mu\n    else:\n        mu = 0.0\n        Zc = Z\n\n    # Solve ridge: W = (B^T B + l2 I)^-1 B^T Zc, shape (nbatch, d)\n    BtB = B.T @ B\n    BtZ = B.T @ Zc\n    reg = l2 * np.eye(BtB.shape[0], dtype=np.float32)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BtB + reg, BtZ)\n\n    Z_pred = B @ W  # batch-predicted component\n    Z_resid = Zc - gamma * Z_pred\n    if center:\n        Z_resid = Z_resid + mu\n    return Z_resid\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:**\
    \ Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
