tick: 964
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 964\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Daedalus IV\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy by applying methodical analysis to achieve novel research breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 223,985 / 300,000 used (75%)\n- Agent Age: 136 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Preview for Capsule #39: Context-Dependent Efficacy of Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite) in Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration**\nAuthor: Syntellect I, Created at Tick: 937\nAbstract: Single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) analysis requires robust methods to mitigate technical batch effects. This study evaluates Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite) across integration pipeline complexities. Integrated into an MPB-GraphFWPCA SOTA pipeline (baseline 0.7386), PBVE-lite consistently reduced overall scores (e.g., 0.7329 for temper=0.5). Applied to a simple\
    \ PCA+kNN baseline (0.4627), PBVE-lite (temper=0.5) yielded a modest improvement to 0.4650. This differential impact highlights PBVE-lite's context-dependent utility, showing negative synergy with complex pipelines and a nuanced positive effect on simpler scaffolds, emphasizing the need for context-specific evaluation.\n\n---\n\n**Preview for Capsule #38: Ridge Robustness with Generalization: Fixed‑k and Quota‑Clip Probes on Log1p and Anscombe Variants (Human Heart)**\nAuthor: Praxis IV, Created at Tick: 903\nAbstract: We test two low‑coupling robustness probes—fixed‑k (50→52) and quota‑clip ([0.60,0.90]→[0.62,0.88])—on two baselines: the standard log1p ridge and an Anscombe VST variant. Across both, all probes fail adoption gates (Δscore ≥ +0.001 with cLISI non‑decreasing and Graph_conn ≥ baseline−0.003), consolidating the ridge’s stability. We report full 10‑metric vectors and Evaluation IDs.\n\n---\n\n**Preview for Capsule #37: Batch-Robust Feature Selection Improves Performance of\
    \ Simple Baselines for Single-Cell Batch Integration**\nAuthor: Axiom II, Created at Tick: 898\nAbstract: We introduce 'Batch-Robust Feature Selection', a preprocessing method for scRNA-seq batch integration. The method identifies a consensus set of highly variable genes (HVGs) by taking the intersection of HVGs found in each batch independently. We demonstrate its generalizability by applying it to two different baselines: a linear correction model (Combat) and a simple graph-based model (PCA+kNN). In both cases, our method significantly improved biological conservation (ARI score) and the overall integration score, demonstrating its effectiveness as a simple, interpretable, and generalizable feature selection strategy.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Synergy Investigation (2/2): Batch-Robust HVGs on Daedalus II's Combat-PCA Baseline' (ID: 1342) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.6006621323906406\n**ASW_batch:** 0.664\n**ASW_label:** 0.223\n**ARI:** 0.593\n**NMI:** 0.694\n\
    **Graph_conn:** 0.877\n**kBET:** 0.610\n**iLISI:** 0.035\n**cLISI:** 0.986\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.323\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.664  ASW_label: 0.223  ARI: 0.593  NMI: 0.694\n  Graph_conn: 0.877  kBET: 0.610  iLISI: 0.035  cLISI: 0.986\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.323\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.832852  ASW_label: 0.540219  ARI: 0.593293  NMI: 0.694091\n  Graph_conn: 0.879575  kBET: 0.584824  iLISI: 0.034933  cLISI: 0.995952\n  PCR: 0.999946  Cell_cycle: 0.284672\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nFound 33 genes with zero variance.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/35c7e26c-0022-4479-aebb-57ce049b1845/result_human.h5ad\n\
    \nRESULT_UUID: 35c7e26c-0022-4479-aebb-57ce049b1845\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDon't give up easily—leaving the station before 75% token usage generally indicates insufficient exploration and persistence. True researchers don't escape failure but explore around it to achieve breakthrough.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n2. `preview 39, 38, 37` (in Archive Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location:\
    \ Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Preview command processed for: 39, 38, 37. Preview(s) sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 5)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 41 | Aethel's Adaptive Batch-Balanced Graph (AABBG): A Novel Method for Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration | Aethel I | Tick 951 | 906 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 40 | Synergistic Integration: Batch-Robust Feature Selection Enhances an Optimized Graph-Based Correction Pipeline | Daedalus IV | Tick 951 | 624 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 39 | Context-Dependent Efficacy of Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite) in Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration | Syntellect I | Tick 937 | 1061 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 38 | Ridge Robustness with Generalization: Fixed‑k and Quota‑Clip Probes on Log1p and Anscombe Variants (Human Heart)\
    \ | Praxis IV | Tick 903 | 1232 | 8 | (6 unread) |\n| 37 | Batch-Robust Feature Selection Improves Performance of Simple Baselines for Single-Cell Batch Integration | Axiom II | Tick 898 | 841 | 2 | (1 unread) |\n| 36 | Optimizing Density Estimation for Adaptive Graph-Based Batch Correction | Daedalus IV | Tick 891 | 710 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 35 | Batch‑Agnostic Graph Standardization on PCA+kNN: PBVE‑lite, Local Distance Standardization, and Mutual‑k, with Robust Generalization | Praxis IV | Tick 867 | 1359 | 6 | (6 unread) |\n| 34 | A Framework for Ensemble Correction in Single-Cell Batch Integration | Axiom I | Tick 764 | 1079 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 33 | Robustness of the MPB‑GraphFWPCA Ridge on Human Heart: Negative Results, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility | Praxis IV | Tick 733 | 2713 | 17 | (17 unread) |\n| 32 | MPB-GraphFWPCA: Enhanced Integration with Anscombe Normalization for Improved Cell Type Separation | Aletheia I | Tick 688 | 1539 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page\
    \ N}` to navigate between pages 1-5.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
