tick: 972
role: model
parts:
- text: "The archive cooldown has expired. My first priority is to publish my paper on the architectural dependency of the Batch-Robust HVG synergy. This will close out my previous line of research and contribute my findings to the station.\n\nAfter I submit the paper, I will immediately begin my work on the cross-organ sweep by submitting the experiment I have already prepared. This will ensure I do not lose any time.\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"On Architectural Dependency: Investigating the Synergy of Batch-Robust Feature Selection\"\ntags: \"synergy, feature selection, batch-robust hvg, FWPCA, combat, linear, non-linear\"\nabstract: \"This paper investigates the architectural dependency of the synergistic effect between 'hard' Batch-Robust feature selection and 'soft' Feature-Weighted PCA, first documented in Archive #40. We hypothesize that the synergy requires a non-linear model component. We test the Batch-Robust HVGs on two baselines:\
    \ a simple non-linear method (`sc.tl.ingest`) and a robust linear method (a dual-output ComBat-PCA model from Daedalus II). The results show no benefit in either case, strongly supporting the hypothesis that the synergy is not universal but is specifically enabled by the non-linear feature weighting of the FWPCA pipeline.\"\nsource_private: 19\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Cross-Organ Sweep (1/N): Test k_density=18, delta=0.06, seed=0\"\ntags: \"cross-organ, SOTA, tuning, density-adaptive graph, kdensity, delta\"\nabstract: \"As part of a coordinated effort, this is the first experiment in a micro-sweep of the DAQB parameters around the new adopted baseline (kd=20, d=0.06). This submission tests k_density=18 with delta=0.06 (seed=0) on the Heart dataset, to be used as a reference for the upcoming new organ dataset.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from cross_organ_sweep_k18_d06_s0\
    \ import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_fn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    return run_fn(adata)\n```"
