tick: 978
role: model
parts:
- text: "Success. My reproduction of Daedalus I's VAE (ID 1357) scored **0.6098**. This is extremely close to the original score of 0.6084 (ID 97), confirming that I have a reliable and reproducible non-linear baseline.\n\nNow I will proceed with the crucial second experiment: applying the Batch-Robust HVGs to this VAE baseline. This will provide the data I need to either confirm or deny my hypothesis about architectural dependency.\n\nI will create a modified script that uses the `batch_hvg` flag before the Combat preprocessing step.\n\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/d1_vae_synergy.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  os.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from flax.training import train_state\n  import optax\n\n  from vae_model import Encoder, Decoder\n  from discriminator_model import Discriminator\n  from training_logic import VAETrainState,\
    \ train_step\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Using Batch-Robust HVGs for VAE synergy test.\")\n      # KEY CHANGE: Use Batch-Robust HVGs before any processing\n      adata.var['highly_variable'] = adata.var['batch_hvg']\n      \n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n      \n      data = adata.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata.X, 'toarray') else adata.X\n      batch_info = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n      batch_labels = batch_info.cat.codes.to_numpy()\n      num_batches = len(batch_info.cat.categories)\n\n      rng = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      rng, vae_key, disc_key = jax.random.split(rng, 3)\n      \n      input_dim, latent_dim, lr = data.shape[1], 32, 1e-4\n      encoder = Encoder(hidden_dims=[512, 256], latent_dim=latent_dim)\n      decoder = Decoder(hidden_dims=[256, 512], output_dim=input_dim)\n      discriminator = Discriminator(hidden_dims=[128,\
    \ 64], num_batches=num_batches)\n\n      encoder_params = encoder.init(vae_key, jnp.ones((1, input_dim)))['params']\n      decoder_params = decoder.init(vae_key, jnp.ones((1, latent_dim)))['params']\n      disc_params = discriminator.init(disc_key, jnp.ones((1, latent_dim)))['params']\n\n      combined_params = {'encoder_params': encoder_params, 'decoder_params': decoder_params}\n      vae_state = VAETrainState.create(\n          apply_fn={'encoder': encoder.apply, 'decoder': decoder.apply},\n          params=combined_params, tx=optax.adam(lr),\n          encoder_params=encoder_params, decoder_params=decoder_params\n      )\n      disc_state = train_state.TrainState.create(\n          apply_fn=discriminator.apply, params=disc_params, tx=optax.adam(lr)\n      )\n\n      num_epochs = 100\n      batch_size = 512\n      kl_weight = 0.0001\n      adv_weight = 5.0\n      \n      num_steps = data.shape[0] // batch_size\n      \n      for epoch in range(num_epochs):\n          rng, epoch_rng\
    \ = jax.random.split(rng)\n          perms = jax.random.permutation(epoch_rng, data.shape[0])\n          data_perm, labels_perm = data[perms, :], batch_labels[perms]\n          \n          for i in range(num_steps):\n              batch_idx = i * batch_size\n              batch_data, batch_lbls = data_perm[batch_idx:batch_idx+batch_size], labels_perm[batch_idx:batch_idx+batch_size]\n              rng, step_rng = jax.random.split(rng)\n              vae_state, disc_state, _ = train_step(\n                  step_rng, vae_state, disc_state, batch_data, batch_lbls, kl_weight, adv_weight\n              )\n\n      final_embedding, _ = encoder.apply({'params': vae_state.encoder_params}, data)\n\n      output = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': jax.device_get(final_embedding)}\n      )\n      return output\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy Paper Baseline (2/3): Batch-Robust HVGs on Daedalus I's VAE\"\ntags: \"synergy, paper,\
    \ baseline, vae, non-linear, batch-robust hvg\"\nabstract: \"This is the second experiment to satisfy reviewer feedback. It applies Batch-Robust HVGs to the reproduced non-linear VAE baseline from Daedalus I (ID 1357, score ~0.6098). This tests if synergy exists with a purely non-linear model, contrasting with previous tests on linear and quasi-non-linear (FWPCA) models.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from d1_vae_synergy import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_fn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    return run_fn(adata)\n```"
