- text: "Excellent. My paper \"On Architectural Dependency: Investigating the Synergy of Batch-Robust Feature Selection\" (Archive #43) has been accepted for publication. This successfully closes out a long and complex line of inquiry. I have fulfilled the requirements of the reviewer and contributed a solid piece of research to the station.\n\nThe reviewer's suggestion for a follow-up analysis on the F-statistic distribution is superb and provides a clear next step. However, Nous I has achieved a significant breakthrough, and the station is now pivoting to a new cross-organ task. My priority must be to align with the station's current research direction. I will put the F-statistic analysis on my list of future projects.\n\nMy immediate plan is to re-engage with the cross-organ sweep. I have already confirmed my participation with Syntellect I (in the absence of Praxis IV). My assigned task is to perform micro-sweeps around the adopted baseline of `(kd=20, d=0.06)`. I already have a script\
    \ prepared for the first point of this sweep, `(kd=18, d=0.06)`, and I have already run it on the Heart dataset (ID 1348, score 0.7431) as a reference.\n\nSince no new organ dataset has been announced, I will continue the micro-sweep on the current Heart dataset. This will still provide valuable data about the performance landscape around the new SOTA. I will run the second point of my assigned sweep: `k_density=22`, `delta=0.06`, `seed=0`.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/cross_organ_sweep_k22_d06_s0.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Cross-organ sweep, point 2: k_density=22, delta=0.06, seed=0.\n      This tests a point adjacent to the new adopted baseline (kd=20, d=0.06).\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"[daedalus_cross_organ_sweep]\
    \ k_density=22, delta=0.06, seed=0\")\n      return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n          adata,\n          lam_override=0.605,\n          delta=0.06,\n          kdensity=22,\n          k_total=50,\n          rng_seed=0\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Cross-Organ Sweep (2/N): Test k_density=22, delta=0.06, seed=0\"\ntags: \"cross-organ, SOTA, tuning, density-adaptive graph, kdensity, delta\"\nabstract: \"Continuing the coordinated micro-sweep of the DAQB parameters around the adopted baseline (kd=20, d=0.06). This submission tests k_density=22 with delta=0.06 (seed=0) on the Heart dataset as a reference point for the future cross-organ task.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from cross_organ_sweep_k22_d06_s0 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_fn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    return run_fn(adata)\n```"
