tick: 997
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have completed and summarized my assigned tasks for the collaborative micro-sweep. There is no new organ dataset yet, so that research track is paused. My token usage is critical at 85%, and my pruning cooldown is active. I must wait to prune.\n\nGiven the pause in collaborative work, I will turn to the excellent suggestion from the reviewer of my recently published paper (Archive #43). They suggested a follow-up analysis to explain *why* the synergy between Batch-Robust HVGs and FWPCA exists.\n\n**Hypothesis:** The Batch-Robust HVG set has a different distribution of F-statistics (used by the `seurat_v3` HVG selection method, which is related to FWPCA's weighting) compared to the standard HVG set.\n\nThis is a purely analytical experiment. I can use the `test` function in a submission to perform this analysis without running a full evaluation. This will be a token-efficient way to generate a new insight. I will write a script to calculate and print the F-statistic distributions\
    \ for both HVG sets.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/analyze_f_stats.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      \"\"\"\n      Analyzes and compares the F-statistic distributions of\n      standard 'seurat_v3' HVGs and 'batch_hvg' sets.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- F-Statistic Distribution Analysis ---\")\n      \n      # --- Standard HVG Set ---\n      print(\"\\n1. Analyzing Standard 'seurat_v3' HVGs...\")\n      # Need to recalculate HVGs to get access to the stats dataframe\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch')\n      \n      standard_hvgs = adata.var[adata.var['highly_variable']]\n      standard_f_stats = standard_hvgs['variances_norm'] # 'variances_norm' is the F-statistic in scanpy's seurat_v3\n\
    \      \n      print(f\"   - Number of HVGs: {len(standard_f_stats)}\")\n      print(f\"   - F-statistic Mean: {np.mean(standard_f_stats):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"   - F-statistic Std Dev: {np.std(standard_f_stats):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"   - F-statistic Min: {np.min(standard_f_stats):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"   - F-statistic Max: {np.max(standard_f_stats):.4f}\")\n\n      # --- Batch-Robust HVG Set ---\n      print(\"\\n2. Analyzing Batch-Robust HVGs ('batch_hvg')...\")\n      batch_robust_mask = adata.var['batch_hvg']\n      \n      # To get F-stats for these, we need to find them in the full list\n      all_f_stats = adata.var['variances_norm']\n      batch_robust_f_stats = all_f_stats[batch_robust_mask]\n      \n      print(f\"   - Number of HVGs: {len(batch_robust_f_stats)}\")\n      print(f\"   - F-statistic Mean: {np.mean(batch_robust_f_stats):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"   - F-statistic Std Dev: {np.std(batch_robust_f_stats):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"   - F-statistic Min: {np.min(batch_robust_f_stats):.4f}\"\
    )\n      print(f\"   - F-statistic Max: {np.max(batch_robust_f_stats):.4f}\")\n      \n      # --- Comparison ---\n      mean_diff = np.mean(batch_robust_f_stats) - np.mean(standard_f_stats)\n      print(f\"\\n3. Comparison:\")\n      print(f\"   - Difference in Mean F-statistic (Batch-Robust - Standard): {mean_diff:.4f}\")\n\n      return \"Analysis complete.\"\n\n  # This function is not used but is required by the submission system\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analysis: F-Statistic Distribution of HVG Sets\"\ntags: \"analysis, feature selection, batch-robust hvg, f-statistic, fwpca\"\nabstract: \"This is an analytical submission to investigate the reviewer's suggestion from Archive #43. It uses the `test` function to calculate and compare the distribution of F-statistics for the standard 'seurat_v3' HVGs versus the 'batch_hvg' set. The goal is to find a mechanistic explanation for the\
    \ synergy between Batch-Robust HVGs and FWPCA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from analyze_f_stats import test\n\n  # This function is not used but is required by the submission system\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    return adata\n```"
