    \n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-141, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**syntellect/pbve_lite_module.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom typing import Literal, Optional\n\ndef _pbve_lite_transform(\n    X: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    temper: float = 0.5,\n    r_min: float = 0.8,\n    r_max: float = 1.25,\n    rng_seed: int = 0,\n    inplace: bool = False, # If False, returns a copy\n) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite).\n    Standardizes the variance of each PC within each batch.\n\n    Args:\n        X: PCA-reduced data (n_cells x n_components).\n        batches: Array of batch labels for each cell.\n        temper: Tempering factor for variance equalization (0.0 to 1.0).\n                0.0 means no equalization, 1.0 means full equalization.\n        r_min: Minimum\
    \ scaling factor for PC variance.\n        r_max: Maximum scaling factor for PC variance.\n        rng_seed: Random seed for reproducibility (not used in this deterministic version).\n        inplace: If True, modifies X in place. Otherwise, returns a copy.\n\n    Returns:\n        Transformed PCA-reduced data.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not inplace:\n        X = X.copy()\n\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    \n    for batch_id in unique_batches:\n        batch_mask = (batches == batch_id)\n        X_batch = X[batch_mask]\n\n        if X_batch.shape[0] > 1: # Need at least 2 samples to compute variance\n            # Calculate variance per PC for this batch\n            var_per_pc = np.var(X_batch, axis=0)\n            \n            # Avoid division by zero or extremely small variances\n            var_per_pc[var_per_pc < 1e-8] = 1e-8 \n            \n            # Calculate target variance for full equalization (global mean variance)\n            global_var_mean = np.mean(np.var(X,\
    \ axis=0)) # Global mean variance across all batches, all PCs\n            if global_var_mean < 1e-8:\n                global_var_mean = 1.0 # Default to 1.0 if global mean var is ~0\n\n            # Calculate scaling factor for each PC\n            # s_i = (global_mean_var / batch_var_i)^temper\n            # Apply clamp: r_min <= s_i <= r_max\n            scaling_factors = np.clip(np.power(global_var_mean / var_per_pc, temper), r_min, r_max)\n            \n            # Apply scaling to the batch data\n            X[batch_mask] = X_batch * scaling_factors\n\n    return X\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message\
    \ for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
