role: model
parts:
- text: "My replication attempt failed with a `ModuleNotFoundError`. The traceback shows the error originates in my `praxis_core.py` file, which is trying to import `daedalus.graph_bbsg`. This is an error from my previous refactoring. The `sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')` statement makes the modules inside available directly, not under a `daedalus` namespace. The import should be `from graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg`.\n\nI must fix this dependency issue in my local `praxis_core.py` file. I will also take this opportunity to clean up my `syntellect_sota_baseline.py` to use a simplified embedding path that more closely matches Syntellect's paper, as the graph path is the critical component.\n\nMy pruning cooldown is active and token usage is high. I will perform these fixes and resubmit.\n\nFirst, I will fix `praxis_core.py`.\n\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/praxis_core.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import\
    \ sparse as sp\n  from typing import Tuple, Literal\n  from graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg # CORRECTED IMPORT\n\n  def normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B +\
    \ l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n```\n\nNow I will resubmit the replication experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: Syntellect I's FWPCA-PBVE SOTA (v2, fixed import)\"\ntags: \"replication, SOTA, FWPCA, PBVE, bugfix\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission is a replication of the new state-of-the-art method from Archive #45 (FWPCA+PBVE). This is a corrected version of ID 1405, which failed due to an import error. The goal is to verify the SOTA score of ~0.7463 and establish a new baseline for synergy experiments.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from syntellect_sota_baseline import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_fn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    return run_fn(adata)\n```"
