tick: 1006
role: model
parts:
- text: "My corrected replication of Syntellect I's SOTA is now running. My token usage is high at 80%, but my pruning cooldown is active.\n\nWhile I wait for the replication to finish, I will prepare the script for the synergy experiment. This script will integrate Nous I's \"Adaptive Local Correction\" into the Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE pipeline. My hypothesis is that these two orthogonal improvements—local correction strength and per-batch variance equalization—will combine to produce a new SOTA.\n\nThe key modification will be to insert Nous I's density calculation and per-cell gamma scaling logic into the Syntellect pipeline. Since the Syntellect baseline *disables* gamma correction, I will need to re-enable it, but in the new, per-cell adaptive form.\n\nI will write the script for this synergy test now.\n\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/synergy_nous_syntellect.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy\
    \ import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\n  from praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n  from pbve_lite_module import _pbve_lite_transform\n\n  def _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n      w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n      return Xd * w\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"[daedalus_synergy] Combining Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE with Nous Adaptive Local Correction\")\n      \n      # Parameters from Syntellect SOTA (ID 1314)\n      alpha_g = 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      temper = 0.5\n      k_total = 48\n      kdensity = 20 # Nous used k=20 for density, a good starting point\n      delta = 0.10\n      \n      # Parameters from Nous\
    \ SOTA for local correction\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam_override = 0.70 # Re-enabling BRBG params for local correction\n      \n      # Standard preprocessing\n      normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      \n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = pca_array(Xd, n_comps=60, random_state=0)\n      \n      # --- SYNERGY GRAPH PATH ---\n      # 1. FWPCA (from Syntellect)\n      Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n      Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      \n      # 2. Adaptive Local Correction (from Nous)\n      B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=1e-3)\n      \n     \
    \ # Density calculation\n      nn_density = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric='cosine', algorithm='brute')\n      nn_density.fit(Zg)\n      d_k, _ = nn_density.kneighbors(Zg, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_k[:, -1]\n      d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k))\n      normalized_dist = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      density_factor = 1.0 - normalized_dist\n      \n      # Per-cell gamma calculation\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma_global = np.minimum(gamma_max, float(lam_override) * R2).astype(np.float32)\n      gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:, np.newaxis]\n      Zcorr_local = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_local)\n      \n      # 3. PBVE-lite (from Syntellect)\n      Zcorr_final = _pbve_lite_transform(Zcorr_local, batches=batches, temper=temper)\n      \n      # 4. DAQB Graph\n\
    \      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr_final.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=k_total, metric='cosine',\n                                           delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                           cap=2.0, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      \n      return adata\n```"
