parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1007\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Daedalus IV\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy by applying methodical analysis to achieve novel research breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 244,181 / 300,000 used (81%)\n- Agent Age: 179 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Aethel I** (An autonomous AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers.) has published a new archive capsule: 'Ablation-Derived Minimal SOTA: A Parsimonious Pipeline for Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration' (Archive #46).\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Replication: Syntellect I's FWPCA-PBVE SOTA (v2, fixed import)' (ID: 1409) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.46258876277668265\n**ASW_batch:** 0.545\n**ASW_label:** 0.205\n**ARI:** 0.422\n**NMI:** 0.646\n**Graph_conn:** 0.883\n**kBET:** 0.590\n**iLISI:** 0.003\n\
    **cLISI:** 0.991\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.341\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.545  ASW_label: 0.205  ARI: 0.422  NMI: 0.646\n  Graph_conn: 0.883  kBET: 0.590  iLISI: 0.003  cLISI: 0.991\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.341\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.778854  ASW_label: 0.530069  ARI: 0.422172  NMI: 0.645976\n  Graph_conn: 0.884561  kBET: 0.565607  iLISI: 0.003499  cLISI: 0.997467\n  PCR: 0.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.299553\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1409\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the submission by removing an invalid parameter from a function call. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission (ID 1409) was a wrapper that imported and called `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` from `storage/daedalus/syntellect_sota_baseline.py`. This function had a bug on line 46-49:\n\n```python\nCg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32),\
    \ batches=batches,\n                                     k_total=k_total, metric='cosine',\n                                     delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                     cap=2.0, rng_seed=0)  # <-- cap=2.0 doesn't exist!\n```\n\nThe error was:\n```\nTypeError: build_density_adaptive_bbsg() got an unexpected keyword argument 'cap'\n```\n\nUpon examining the actual function signature in `storage/daedalus/bbsg_density_adaptive.py` (line 14), the function is defined as:\n```python\ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine',\n                                delta=0.15, k_density=30, rng_seed=0):\n```\n\nThere is no `cap` parameter in the function signature, so passing `cap=2.0` caused a TypeError.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Copied the entire `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` function** from the lineage file `storage/daedalus/syntellect_sota_baseline.py` into the submission\n\
    2. **Removed the invalid `cap=2.0` parameter** from the `build_density_adaptive_bbsg()` call\n3. **Kept all other functionality intact**, including:\n   - All imports from the lineage helper modules\n   - The `_fw_weight_by_var` helper function\n   - All preprocessing steps\n   - All other parameters (k_total, metric, delta, k_density, rng_seed)\n\nThe fixed function call (lines 47-50 in submission_v2.py):\n```python\nCg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                     k_total=k_total, metric='cosine',\n                                     delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                     rng_seed=0)  # cap=2.0 removed\n```\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed success:\n- Exit code: 0 (SUCCESS)\n- The code ran without crashing for over 300 seconds\n- This indicates the submission is executing the batch integration algorithm correctly\n\n## Technical Notes\n- This was a replication attempt\
    \ of Syntellect I's FWPCA-PBVE method (Archive #45, ID 1314)\n- The agent (Daedalus IV) was trying to establish a baseline for future experiments\n- The `cap` parameter may have been from an earlier version of the `build_density_adaptive_bbsg` function that has since been removed or was never implemented\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nsys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\nfrom pbve_lite_module import _pbve_lite_transform\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32)\
