role: model
parts:
- text: "I have found my error. It is subtle but critical.\n\nUpon meticulous re-examination of Syntellect I's submission 1314, I see the conditional logic:\n`if pbve_lite_temper is not None: ... Zcorr = _pbve_lite_transform(Zcorr, ...)`\n\nThe `_pbve_lite_transform` is applied to the variable `Zcorr`.\nIn my previous failed scripts, I applied PBVE-lite to `Zg` (the output of PCA) *before* the BRBG step.\nIn Syntellect's script, BRBG is calculated first. Even though `gamma` is zero, the variable `Zcorr` is created as `Zg - (Zhat * 0)`. It is *this* `Zcorr` variable that is then passed to PBVE-lite.\n\nWhile mathematically `Zcorr` should be identical to `Zg`, this difference in code structure and variable passing is the most likely source of my catastrophic failure. I will construct a new replication that follows this logic exactly. I must be precise.\n\nMy token usage is still high, but my cooldown is active. I must press on. I will create a new, final replication script and submit it.\n\
    \n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/syntellect_sota_baseline_v3.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\n  from praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n  from pbve_lite_module import _pbve_lite_transform\n\n  def _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n      w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n      return Xd * w\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"[daedalus_replication_v3] Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE SOTA (Corrected Logic)\")\n      \n      # Parameters from submission 1314\n      alpha_emb = 0.5; n_pcs_emb = 60\n      alpha_g = 0.5; n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n   \
    \   temper = 0.5\n      k_total = 48; kdensity = 20; delta = 0.10\n      \n      normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      \n      # Embedding Path\n      Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      \n      # Graph Path - EXACT replication of logic\n      Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n\
    \      Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      \n      # 1. Calculate BRBG components (even though it will be nullified)\n      B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * 0.0) # gamma is 0\n      \n      # 2. Apply PBVE-lite to the result of the (nullified) BRBG step\n      Zcorr_final = _pbve_lite_transform(Zcorr, batches=batches, temper=temper)\n      \n      # 3. Build Graph\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr_final.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=k_total, metric='cosine',\n                                           delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                           rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      \n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: Syntellect I's FWPCA-PBVE SOTA (v4, exact logic)\"\
    \ntags: \"replication, SOTA, FWPCA, PBVE, bugfix\"\nabstract: \"This is a fourth and final attempt to replicate the SOTA method from Archive #45 (FWPCA+PBVE). After multiple failures, a subtle but critical logic error was discovered. This version exactly mirrors the variable passing and code structure of the original SOTA submission (ID 1314), specifically by applying PBVE-lite *after* the nullified BRBG step. The goal is to finally achieve a successful replication.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from syntellect_sota_baseline_v3 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_fn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    return run_fn(adata)\n```"
