tick: 1014
role: model
parts:
- text: "My final replication attempt (ID 1418) has failed, scoring an abysmal **0.6249**. This is identical to the previous failure, confirming the logic error is deep and I have not yet found it. I have been systematically failing to replicate the FWPCA+PBVE SOTA. The `iLISI` score of 0.023 shows a complete failure of batch integration.\n\nI have exhausted my ability to debug this by simple inspection. I am missing a fundamental piece of information. The problem is not a simple typo; it is a conceptual misunderstanding of the pipeline.\n\nI will now take a step back and adopt a more rigorous debugging strategy. I will use the `test()` function to print out intermediate data structures and compare them to a known working implementation. Syntellect I's original SOTA submission is ID 1314. I will run a `test` function on both my broken implementation and their successful one, printing the shapes and sums of key matrices (`Zg`, `Zcorr`). This will allow me to pinpoint exactly where my pipeline\
    \ diverges.\n\nFirst, I will create a debug script for my broken implementation.\n\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/debug_syntellect_rep.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # This is my broken replication script, with a test() function added.\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\n  from praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\n  from pbve_lite_module import _pbve_lite_transform\n\n  def _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n      w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n      return Xd * w\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      print(\"[DAEDALUS DEBUG] Running diagnostic test on my broken replication.\")\n      \n      alpha_g = 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      temper = 0.5\n      \n     \
    \ normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      \n      Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n      Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      print(f\"[DAEDALUS DEBUG] Zg shape: {Zg.shape}, Zg sum: {np.sum(Zg):.4f}\")\n      \n      B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      Zcorr_brbg_disabled = Zg - (Zhat * 0.0)\n      \n      Zcorr_final = _pbve_lite_transform(Zcorr_brbg_disabled, batches=batches, temper=temper)\n      print(f\"[DAEDALUS DEBUG] Zcorr_final shape: {Zcorr_final.shape}, Zcorr_final sum: {np.sum(Zcorr_final):.4f}\")\n      \n      return \"Debug analysis\
    \ complete.\"\n```\n\nNow, I will submit this for a test run.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Debug (1/2): My Broken Syntellect SOTA Replication\"\ntags: \"debug, replication, SOTA, FWPCA, PBVE\"\nabstract: \"This is a non-scoring test run to debug my failed replications of Syntellect I's SOTA (ID 1418, score 0.6249). This submission runs my broken code in test mode to print the shape and sum of key intermediate matrices (Zg, Zcorr_final) for comparison.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from debug_syntellect_rep import test\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      # This function will not be called because test() is defined.\n      pass\n```"
