- text: "Several key events have occurred.\n\n1.  **Nous SOTA Replication:** My replication of Nous I's SOTA (ID 1451) was a success. The score is **0.7448**. This is a strong result, very close to Nous I's seed 0 run of 0.7454. This confirms my ability to reproduce the method and provides a new, powerful baseline for my own research.\n\n2.  **Praxis V Paper:** I have read Archive #48. Praxis V's finding that the optimal `delta` is topology-dependent is a crucial insight. It explains why my attempt to tune `delta` on the SOTA model was not as impactful as Nous I's tuning on their modified pipeline.\n\n3.  **Praxis V Public Memory:** I have read the summary, which aligns with the paper. The collaborative phase of the 2D sweep is now fully concluded.\n\nMy meta-prompt goal to replicate Nous I's SOTA is complete. It is time to set a new direction.\n\n**New Goal:** The clear next step is to test for synergy between the two new SOTA methods: **Nous I's \"Adaptive Local Correction\"** and **Syntellect\
    \ I's \"FWPCA-PBVE\" pipeline**. My failed attempts to replicate the Syntellect SOTA are a significant obstacle. However, Syntellect's paper (Archive #47) provides a clear implementation. I must try one more time, with extreme care, to replicate Syntellect's `FWPCA-Only SOTA Baseline (BRBG Disabled)` (ID 1339, score 0.7421). This is a simpler baseline than their full SOTA, and replicating it is a necessary first step.\n\nI will set a new meta prompt and begin this new line of inquiry.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **NEW GOAL: SYNERGY TEST**\n  1. Replicate Syntellect I's **FWPCA-Only SOTA Baseline (BRBG Disabled)** from Archive #47 (ID 1339, score 0.7421). BE METICULOUS.\n  2. If successful, integrate Nous I's \"Adaptive Local Correction\" to test for synergy.\n```\n\nNow, I will return to the Research Counter to begin this final, careful attempt at replication. I will start by reviewing Syntellect's paper again to extract the exact parameters.\n\n/execute_action{goto\
    \ archive}\n/execute_action{read 47}"
