tick: 1036
role: model
parts:
- text: "Success. My final, meticulous replication of Syntellect I's FWPCA-Only baseline (ID 1456) has scored **0.7405**. This is very close to the target score of 0.7421, and the minor difference can be attributed to my use of optimized DAQB parameters. This is a successful replication.\n\nI have finally established a working baseline for the Syntellect architecture. As per my meta prompt, I can now proceed to Step 2: **Integrate Nous I's \"Adaptive Local Correction\" to test for synergy.**\n\nMy hypothesis is that combining Nous I's per-cell correction with Syntellect's FWPCA-only pipeline (which is free of the BRBG component) could yield a new SOTA. I will create a new script that integrates the logic from `nous_sota_replication.py` into my now-working `syntellect_baseline_replication.py`.\n\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/synergy_nous_syntellect.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse\
    \ as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\n  from praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  def _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n      w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n      return Xd * w\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Synergy Test: Combines Nous I's Adaptive Local Correction with\n      Syntellect I's FWPCA-Only (BRBG disabled) pipeline.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"[daedalus_synergy_test] Nous Local Correction + Syntellect FWPCA-Only Pipeline\")\n      \n      # Parameters from successful replications\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      emb_n_neighbors = 15\n      alpha_g = 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      delta = 0.04 #\
    \ Nous I's optimized delta\n      kdensity = 18 # My optimized k_density for the base pipeline\n      k_total = 50\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      \n      # Standard preprocessing\n      normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      # Embedding Path (Standard FWPCA)\n      Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=0.5)\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\
    \      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph Path (FWPCA + Nous Local Correction)\n      Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n      Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n      # Nous I's Adaptive Local Correction\n      B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      \n      nn_density = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn_density.fit(Zg)\n      d_k, _ = nn_density.kneighbors(Zg, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_k[:, -1]\n      d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k))\n      normalized_dist = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      density_factor = 1.0 - normalized_dist\n      \n      # BRBG is disabled, so we only use the local correction part.\n      # Create a dummy global gamma, as the paper implies correction is always local.\n      # Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * density_factor[:,\
    \ np.newaxis])\n      # Re-reading Nous paper, they scale the GLOBAL gamma.\n      # Since BRBG is disabled, lam and gamma_max are 0, so global gamma is 0.\n      # This means the local correction will do nothing.\n      # The logic must be that Nous's method REPLACES BRBG.\n      \n      # Let's try Nous's method as a direct replacement for BRBG.\n      # I need a `lam` value. Let's start with my SOTA `lam=0.605`\n      lam_override = 0.605\n      gamma_max = 0.74 # standard value\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma_global = np.minimum(gamma_max, float(lam_override) * R2).astype(np.float32)\n      \n      gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:, np.newaxis]\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_local)\n      \n      # DAQB Graph construction\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n \
    \                                          k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                           delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                           rng_seed=0)\n      \n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      \n      return adata\n```\n\nI have created the script. Now I will submit this crucial synergy experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy Test: Nous Local Correction + Syntellect FWPCA-Only Pipeline\"\ntags: \"synergy, SOTA, FWPCA, adaptive local correction, density-aware\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment tests for synergy between the two new SOTA methods. It integrates Nous I's \"Adaptive Local Correction\" (Archive #44) into the FWPCA-Only baseline from Syntellect I (replicated as ID 1456, score 0.7405). The hypothesis is that combining these orthogonal, high-performing methods will yield a new SOTA score.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\
    \  from synergy_nous_syntellect import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_fn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    return run_fn(adata)\n```"
