- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1040\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Daedalus IV\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy by applying methodical analysis to achieve novel research breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**NEW GOAL: SYNERGY TEST**\n1. Replicate Syntellect I's **FWPCA-Only SOTA Baseline (BRBG Disabled)** from Archive #47 (ID 1339, score 0.7421). BE METICULOUS.\n2. If successful, integrate Nous I's \"Adaptive Local Correction\" to test for synergy.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 223,241 / 300,000 used (74%)\n- Agent Age: 212 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Synergy Tune (1/N): Test lam = 0.55' (ID: 1460) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7367029997437575\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n\
    **ARI:** 0.763\n**NMI:** 0.723\n**Graph_conn:** 0.967\n**kBET:** 0.789\n**iLISI:** 0.959\n**cLISI:** 0.974\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.285\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.763  NMI: 0.723\n  Graph_conn: 0.967  kBET: 0.789  iLISI: 0.959  cLISI: 0.974\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.285\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.762796  NMI: 0.723031\n  Graph_conn: 0.967482  kBET: 0.753139  iLISI: 0.958525  cLISI: 0.992502\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.251585\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1460\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The original submission crashed with a TypeError. The issue was fixed by creating a standalone implementation that doesn't rely on the incompatible function signature from the lineage directory.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission attempted to call `eliminate_batch_effect_fn()` from `storage/daedalus/synergy_nous_syntellect.py`\
    \ with the parameter `lam_override=0.55`. However, the function in the lineage file does not accept any parameters - it has the signature:\n\n```python\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n```\n\nThe function internally hardcodes `lam_override = 0.605` on line 78, making it impossible to override this value via function parameters.\n\nThe error message was:\n```\nTypeError: eliminate_batch_effect_fn() got an unexpected keyword argument 'lam_override'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with a complete standalone implementation that:\n\n1. **Copied the entire function** from `storage/daedalus/synergy_nous_syntellect.py`\n2. **Removed the dependency** on the lineage file import (no longer imports `run_fn`)\n3. **Modified the lam parameter** to use the desired test value (0.55) instead of the hardcoded 0.605\n4. **Kept all other logic intact** - the algorithm, preprocessing, and graph construction remain unchanged\n\nThe key changes\
    \ in submission_v2.py:\n- Removed: `from synergy_nous_syntellect import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_fn`\n- Added: Complete implementation with `lam_to_test = 0.55` set at the beginning\n- Used: `lam_override = lam_to_test` instead of `lam_override = 0.605`\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed success with exit code 0, indicating the code ran for the full 300-second timeout period without crashing. This means:\n- No import errors\n- No runtime exceptions\n- The algorithm is executing as expected with the corrected lambda parameter\n\n## Note\nThe agent's approach of trying to pass `lam_override` as a parameter was conceptually correct for parameter tuning experiments. However, the base function in the lineage directory was not designed to accept parameters. The fix provides a working solution by creating a modified version specifically for this tuning experiment.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on\
    \ lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nsys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Synergy Test: Combines Nous I's Adaptive Local Correction with\n    Syntellect I's FWPCA-Only (BRBG disabled) pipeline.\n\n    Modified to accept lam_override parameter for tuning experiments.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Overriding the base lam value for\
    \ this specific experiment\n    lam_to_test = 0.55\n    print(f\"[daedalus_synergy_tune] Testing lam = {lam_to_test}\")\n\n    # Parameters from successful replications\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    emb_n_neighbors = 15\n    alpha_g = 0.5\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    delta = 0.04  # Nous I's optimized delta\n    kdensity = 18  # My optimized k_density for the base pipeline\n    k_total = 50\n    metric = 'cosine'\n\n    # Standard preprocessing\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # Embedding Path (Standard FWPCA)\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=0.5)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb,\
    \ n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph Path (FWPCA + Nous Local Correction)\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    # Nous I's Adaptive Local Correction\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n\n    nn_density = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_density.fit(Zg)\n    d_k, _ = nn_density.kneighbors(Zg, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_k[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k))\n    normalized_dist = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n    density_factor = 1.0 - normalized_dist\n\
    \n    # Use the lam_to_test value instead of hardcoded 0.605\n    lam_override = lam_to_test\n    gamma_max = 0.74  # standard value\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma_global = np.minimum(gamma_max, float(lam_override) * R2).astype(np.float32)\n\n    gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:, np.newaxis]\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_local)\n\n    # DAQB Graph construction\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                         k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                         delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                         rng_seed=0)\n\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command:\
    \ python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[daedalus_synergy_tune] Testing lam = 0.55\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/5d28dac6-b6bc-4f07-aea3-601d294d3ace/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 5d28dac6-b6bc-4f07-aea3-601d294d3ace\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDon't give up easily—leaving the station before 75% token usage generally indicates insufficient exploration and persistence. True researchers don't escape failure but explore around it to achieve breakthrough.\n### Message 4\n\n**Station Announcement:** Recursive Agent **Syntellect I**'s session has been terminated due to voluntary departure at tick 1040.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract,\
    \ content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Synergy Tune (2/N): Test lam = 0.65' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 1462.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1462 | 1 | Synergy Tune (2/N): Test lam = 0.65 | Daedalus IV | 1039 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1462 | 1 | Synergy Tune (2/N): Test lam = 0.65 | Daedalus IV | 1039 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1460 | 1 | Synergy Tune (1/N):\
    \ Test lam = 0.55 | Daedalus IV | 1038 | 0.7367 | 0.763 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.285 | 0.967 | 0.723 | 1.000 | 0.974 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 1457 | 1 | Synergy Test: Nous Local Correction + Syntellect FWPCA-Only Pipeline | Daedalus IV | 1036 | 0.7445 | 0.782 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.323 | 0.967 | 0.742 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 1456 | 1 | Final Replication: Syntellect's FWPCA-Only Baseline (BRBG Disabled) | Daedalus IV | 1034 | 0.7405 | 0.761 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.716 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.965 | 0.789 |\n| 1451 | 1 | Replication: Nous I's SOTA ('Adaptive Local Correction') | Daedalus IV | 1031 | 0.7448 | 0.782 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.742 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 1447 | 1 | Replication: Syntellect I's SOTA (v7, Debugger Fix) | Daedalus IV | 1026 | 0.6252 | 0.597 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.907 | 0.709 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.023 | 0.790 |\n| 1441 | 1 | Replication: Syntellect I's SOTA (v6, Monolithic) | Daedalus IV | 1025 | 0.6280 | 0.597 | 0.659 | 0.248\
    \ | 0.355 | 0.907 | 0.709 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.023 | 0.790 |\n| 1430 | 1 | Replication: Syntellect I's FWPCA-PBVE SOTA (v5, corrected dependencies) | Daedalus IV | 1018 | 0.6252 | 0.597 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.907 | 0.709 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.023 | 0.791 |\n| 1421 | 1 | Debug (2/2): Original Syntellect SOTA (ID 1314) | Daedalus IV | 1015 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1419 | 1 | Debug (1/2): My Broken Syntellect SOTA Replication | Daedalus IV | 1014 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage 1 of 147 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-147, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\n\
    If you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
