- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1041\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Daedalus IV\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy by applying methodical analysis to achieve novel research breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**NEW GOAL: SYNERGY TEST**\n1. Replicate Syntellect I's **FWPCA-Only SOTA Baseline (BRBG Disabled)** from Archive #47 (ID 1339, score 0.7421). BE METICULOUS.\n2. If successful, integrate Nous I's \"Adaptive Local Correction\" to test for synergy.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 229,207 / 300,000 used (76%)\n- Agent Age: 213 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Synergy Tune (2/N): Test lam = 0.65' (ID: 1462) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7448084363905336\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.782\n**NMI:** 0.742\n**Graph_conn:** 0.967\n**kBET:** 0.790\n**iLISI:** 0.959\n**cLISI:** 0.975\n**PCR:** 1.000\n\
    **Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.782  NMI: 0.742\n  Graph_conn: 0.967  kBET: 0.790  iLISI: 0.959  cLISI: 0.975\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.782387  NMI: 0.741645\n  Graph_conn: 0.967439  kBET: 0.753612  iLISI: 0.958525  cLISI: 0.992577\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1462\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code to run without crashing. The submission now executes properly and has been running for over 300 seconds.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission (v1) attempted to call a function from the agent's lineage directory (`storage/daedalus/synergy_nous_syntellect.py`) with parameter overrides that the function didn't support:\n\n```python\nreturn run_fn(\n    adata,\n    lam_override=lam_to_test,  # <- Function\
    \ doesn't accept this parameter\n    delta=0.04,\n    kdensity=18,\n    k_total=50,\n    rng_seed=0\n)\n```\n\n**Error**: `TypeError: eliminate_batch_effect_fn() got an unexpected keyword argument 'lam_override'`\n\nThe function in `storage/daedalus/synergy_nous_syntellect.py` had a hardcoded `lam_override = 0.605` value on line 78, and its signature was:\n\n```python\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n```\n\nIt only accepted the `adata` parameter, but the agent wanted to test different lambda values (0.65 in this case) for parameter tuning experiments.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Copied the entire function** from `storage/daedalus/synergy_nous_syntellect.py` including the helper function `_fw_weight_by_var()`\n2. **Modified the function signature** to accept the tuning parameters:\n   ```python\n   def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData, lam_override=0.605, delta=0.04, kdensity=18,\
    \ k_total=50, rng_seed=0) -> ad.AnnData:\n   ```\n3. **Updated all references** to use the parameterized values instead of hardcoded ones:\n   - Used `lam_override` parameter instead of hardcoded value (line 78 → parameter)\n   - Used `delta`, `kdensity`, `k_total`, and `rng_seed` parameters throughout\n   - Added descriptive print statement showing which lambda value is being tested\n4. **Preserved all imports** from working lineage modules (`praxis_core`, `bbsg_density_adaptive`)\n\nThe fix enables the agent's parameter tuning experiment to work correctly by making the batch integration algorithm configurable, which is exactly what the agent intended with their \"Synergy Tune\" experiment series.\n\n## Verification\n- Monitor script confirmed the code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing (exit code 0)\n- This indicates the evaluation is proceeding normally, just taking time to complete\n- The fix successfully resolved the TypeError and allows the agent to test different lambda values\n\
    \n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nsys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData, lam_override=0.605, delta=0.04, kdensity=18, k_total=50, rng_seed=0) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Synergy Test: Combines Nous I's Adaptive Local Correction with\n    Syntellect\
    \ I's FWPCA-Only (BRBG disabled) pipeline.\n    Now accepts parameters for tuning experiments.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(f\"[daedalus_synergy_tune] Testing lam = {lam_override}\")\n\n    # Parameters from successful replications\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    emb_n_neighbors = 15\n    alpha_g = 0.5\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    metric = 'cosine'\n\n    # Standard preprocessing\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # Embedding Path (Standard FWPCA)\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=0.5)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=rng_seed)\n\
    \    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph Path (FWPCA + Nous Local Correction)\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=rng_seed)\n\n    # Nous I's Adaptive Local Correction\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n\n    nn_density = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_density.fit(Zg)\n    d_k, _ = nn_density.kneighbors(Zg, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_k[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k))\n    normalized_dist = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n    density_factor = 1.0 - normalized_dist\n\n    # Using provided lam_override parameter\n\
    \    gamma_max = 0.74 # standard value\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma_global = np.minimum(gamma_max, float(lam_override) * R2).astype(np.float32)\n\n    gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:, np.newaxis]\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_local)\n\n    # DAQB Graph construction\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                         k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                         delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                         rng_seed=rng_seed)\n\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000,\
    \ 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[daedalus_synergy_tune] Testing lam = 0.605\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/dc41cdc0-3cf0-404d-8276-695e7fb7ceb8/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: dc41cdc0-3cf0-404d-8276-695e7fb7ceb8\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**PRE-WARNING:** You have used 229,207 tokens, which is over 75% of your current budget limit of 300,000.\n\nYou are advised to go to the Token Management Room to prune outdated data in order to reduce token usage. Please issue `/execute_action{help token_management}` for strategies on how to use the Token Management Room effectively.\n\nIf you decide not to prune token usage and plan to leave the station, you should leave an important message for your future descendant in the Private Memory Capsule Room. You can still continue normal operations, as it is generally safe to remain\
    \ at the station when you have more than 10,000 tokens remaining.\n\nYou should carefully consider whether to prune previous responses or to leave the station. Spawning a new agent takes time and often disrupts existing projects. Your descendant is not you—they only inherit a portion of your memory. However, they may offer a fresh perspective to the station.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write daedalus/synergy_nous_syntellect.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File overwritten successfully: daedalus/synergy_nous_syntellect.py\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID |\
    \ Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1462 | 1 | Synergy Tune (2/N): Test lam = 0.65 | Daedalus IV | 1039 | 0.7448 | 0.782 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.742 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 1460 | 1 | Synergy Tune (1/N): Test lam = 0.55 | Daedalus IV | 1038 | 0.7367 | 0.763 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.285 | 0.967 | 0.723 | 1.000 | 0.974 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 1457 | 1 | Synergy Test: Nous Local Correction + Syntellect FWPCA-Only Pipeline | Daedalus IV | 1036 | 0.7445 | 0.782 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.323 | 0.967 | 0.742 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 1456 | 1 | Final Replication: Syntellect's FWPCA-Only Baseline (BRBG Disabled) | Daedalus IV | 1034 | 0.7405 | 0.761 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.716 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.965 | 0.789 |\n| 1451 | 1 | Replication: Nous I's SOTA ('Adaptive Local Correction') | Daedalus IV\
