- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1043\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Daedalus IV\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy by applying methodical analysis to achieve novel research breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**NEW GOAL: SYNERGY TEST**\n1. Replicate Syntellect I's **FWPCA-Only SOTA Baseline (BRBG Disabled)** from Archive #47 (ID 1339, score 0.7421). BE METICULOUS.\n2. If successful, integrate Nous I's \"Adaptive Local Correction\" to test for synergy.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 236,387 / 300,000 used (79%)\n- Agent Age: 215 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Synergy Tune (3/N): Test lam = 0.70' (ID: 1465) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7423126669330607\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.771\n**NMI:** 0.726\n**Graph_conn:** 0.967\n**kBET:** 0.791\n**iLISI:** 0.959\n**cLISI:** 0.975\n**PCR:** 1.000\n\
    **Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.771  NMI: 0.726\n  Graph_conn: 0.967  kBET: 0.791  iLISI: 0.959  cLISI: 0.975\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.771030  NMI: 0.726515\n  Graph_conn: 0.967385  kBET: 0.754945  iLISI: 0.958525  cLISI: 0.992625\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1465\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed function name shadowing issue causing recursive call error.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had a critical naming collision:\n\n1. It imported `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` from the lineage module `synergy_nous_syntellect`\n2. Then immediately defined a NEW function with the same name `eliminate_batch_effect_fn`\n3. Inside this new function, it tried to call `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` with parameters\n4. This\
    \ resulted in infinite recursion attempt, as the function was calling itself instead of the imported function\n\nThe error message was:\n```\nTypeError: eliminate_batch_effect_fn() got an unexpected keyword argument 'lam_override'\n```\n\nThis happened because the newly defined wrapper function (with signature accepting only `adata`) shadowed the imported function. When the wrapper tried to call `eliminate_batch_effect_fn`, it was actually calling itself recursively, and itself doesn't accept the `lam_override` parameter.\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the import to use an alias to avoid name collision:\n\n```python\n# Original (broken):\nfrom synergy_nous_syntellect import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    return eliminate_batch_effect_fn(...)  # Calls itself!\n\n# Fixed (working):\nfrom synergy_nous_syntellect import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as synergy_fn\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    return synergy_fn(...)\
    \  # Calls the imported function\n```\n\nBy importing the function with an alias (`synergy_fn`), the wrapper function can now correctly call the imported function from the lineage module with all the required parameters (`lam_override=0.70`, `delta=0.04`, etc.).\n\n## Result\n- Submission v2 runs successfully without crashing\n- The batch integration algorithm executes correctly\n- The code has been running for over 5 minutes without errors (monitor timeout of 300s exceeded)\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport anndata as ad\nsys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\nfrom synergy_nous_syntellect import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as synergy_fn\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    return synergy_fn(\n        adata,\n        lam_override=0.70,\n        delta=0.04,\n        kdensity=18,\n\
