tick: 1048
role: model
parts:
- text: "My paper has been rejected for lacking a generalization test. This is a recurring and critical lesson for me. A finding, no matter how strong, is incomplete without proof of its robustness. The reviewer has provided a clear path forward: apply my new synergistic method to the simple ComBat baseline used by Nous I.\n\nMy plan is now clear and urgent:\n1.  **Replicate the Simple Baseline:** First, I must replicate the simple `PCA -> ComBat` baseline that Nous I used (ID 1377, score 0.4548) to establish a starting point.\n2.  **Run Generalization Test:** Apply my new method (FWPCA-Only + Local Correction with `lam=0.65`) to this simple baseline.\n3.  **Update and Resubmit Paper:** Incorporate these two new experiments into my paper and resubmit it to the archive.\n\nI will begin by creating the script to replicate the simple Combat baseline.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/simple_combat_baseline.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import\
    \ anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  \n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Replication of the simple PCA -> ComBat baseline used by Nous I\n      in Archive #44 (ID 1377).\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"[daedalus_gen_test] Running simple Combat baseline.\")\n      \n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', subset=True)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=50)\n      sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n      \n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.X.copy()\n      \n      # Remove graph to match the baseline's output\n      if 'connectivities' in adata.obsp:\n          del adata.obsp['connectivities']\n      if 'distances' in adata.obsp:\n          del adata.obsp['distances']\n          \n      return adata\n```\n\nNow, I will submit this baseline replication.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy Paper Gen. Test\
    \ (1/2): Replicate Simple Combat Baseline\"\ntags: \"generalization, synergy, baseline, combat\"\nabstract: \"As required by reviewer feedback for a paper on a new synergistic method, this submission replicates the simple PCA->ComBat baseline used by Nous I (Archive #44, ID 1377). This will establish the starting point for a generalization test. Expected score is ~0.4548.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from simple_combat_baseline import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_fn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    return run_fn(adata)\n```"
