tick: 1049
role: model
parts:
- text: "My baseline replication for the generalization test is running. While I wait, I will prepare the script for the second part of the test: applying my synergistic model to this simple Combat baseline.\n\nThis requires careful thought. My full synergistic model includes an FWPCA step, an Adaptive Local Correction step, and a DAQB graph construction. Applying all of this to the simple Combat output would not be a clean test. The reviewer's suggestion was to demonstrate that the *synergy* is robust. The core synergy I discovered is between the **FWPCA-Only (BRBG-disabled) pipeline** and **Nous I's Adaptive Local Correction**.\n\nTherefore, the proper generalization test is to take the simple Combat baseline's core idea—a PCA'd embedding corrected by ComBat—and then *replace* its output with a graph constructed using my full synergistic pipeline. This is too complex.\n\nA simpler interpretation, aligned with Nous I's own generalization test, is to take a simple baseline and add the new\
    \ component. Nous I added \"Adaptive Local Correction\" to a simple Combat pipeline. I will do the same, but with my *synergistic combination*. My combination involves FWPCA and Adaptive Local Correction. So, I will add both to the simple `PCA -> Combat` framework. Since `Combat` works on the PCA space, and my method also corrects the PCA space, I cannot run them sequentially.\n\nLet's re-read Nous I's paper. They replaced the ComBat correction with their Local Adaptive Correction. That is the correct experimental design.\n\nSo, the experiment will be:\n1. Normalize and select HVGs.\n2. Run PCA.\n3. Apply my synergistic correction (FWPCA-Only logic + Local Correction) to the PCA space.\n4. Output the corrected embedding.\n\nThis is a clean test of my method on a simple scaffold, exactly what the reviewer asked for.\n\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/synergy_gen_test2_final.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as\
    \ ad\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\n  from praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\n\n  def _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n      w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n      return Xd * w\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Synergy Paper Gen. Test (2/2): Apply synergistic method to a simple baseline.\n      Replaces ComBat in a simple PCA pipeline with the FWPCA-Only + Local Correction method.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"[daedalus_gen_test] Applying synergistic correction to simple PCA baseline.\")\n      \n      # Parameters for the synergistic method\n      alpha_g = 0.5\n      n_comps_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam_override = 0.65 # My optimized lambda\n      kdensity =\
    \ 20 # Using Nous's kdensity for their baseline\n      \n      # Standard preprocessing\n      normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      # FWPCA step\n      Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n      Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_comps_graph, random_state=0)\n\n      # Nous I's Adaptive Local Correction logic\n      B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      nn_density = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric='cosine', algorithm='brute')\n      nn_density.fit(Zg)\n      d_k, _ = nn_density.kneighbors(Zg, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_k[:, -1]\n      d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)),\
    \ float(np.max(d_k))\n      normalized_dist = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      density_factor = 1.0 - normalized_dist\n      \n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma_global = np.minimum(gamma_max, float(lam_override) * R2).astype(np.float32)\n      gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:, np.newaxis]\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_local)\n      \n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zcorr\n      \n      return adata\n```"
