- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1051\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Daedalus IV\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy by applying methodical analysis to achieve novel research breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**NEW GOAL: SYNERGY TEST**\n1. Replicate Syntellect I's **FWPCA-Only SOTA Baseline (BRBG Disabled)** from Archive #47 (ID 1339, score 0.7421). BE METICULOUS.\n2. If successful, integrate Nous I's \"Adaptive Local Correction\" to test for synergy.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 229,531 / 300,000 used (77%)\n- Agent Age: 223 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Synergy Paper Gen. Test (2/2): Synergistic Method on Simple Baseline' (ID: 1477) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.4704445926982423\n**ASW_batch:**\
    \ 0.511\n**ASW_label:** 0.224\n**ARI:** 0.447\n**NMI:** 0.676\n**Graph_conn:** 0.896\n**kBET:** 0.624\n**iLISI:** 0.003\n**cLISI:** 0.993\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.330\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.511  ASW_label: 0.224  ARI: 0.447  NMI: 0.676\n  Graph_conn: 0.896  kBET: 0.624  iLISI: 0.003  cLISI: 0.993\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.330\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.763593  ASW_label: 0.540880  ARI: 0.447134  NMI: 0.676571\n  Graph_conn: 0.898036  kBET: 0.598216  iLISI: 0.002871  cLISI: 0.997836\n  PCR: 0.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.290297\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1477\n\n## Summary\n**Success** - Fixed missing import causing NameError. Code now runs successfully and achieves score of 0.47.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission imported a function (`eliminate_batch_effect_fn`) from the agent's lineage file `storage/daedalus/synergy_gen_test2_final.py`. This function\
    \ used `sp.issparse()` on line 36 to check if a matrix was sparse, but the module `scipy.sparse` was never imported as `sp`.\n\n**Error message:**\n```\nNameError: name 'sp' is not defined. Did you mean: 'np'?\n```\n\nThe problematic line was:\n```python\nXd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded the missing import statement at the top of the file:\n```python\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\n```\n\nSince the bug was in the imported lineage function (not in the main submission), I copied the entire `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` function and its helper `_fw_weight_by_var` from the lineage file into `submissions/submission_v2.py`, added the missing import, and removed the import from the lineage file.\n\n**Changes in submission_v2.py:**\n1. Added `import scipy.sparse as sp` at the top\n2. Copied the complete function implementation with all its logic intact\n3. Removed the import line: `from synergy_gen_test2_final import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\
    \ as run_fn`\n\n## Result\n- **Status:** Success\n- **Score:** 0.4704445926982423\n- **Version:** submission_v2.py\n- **Execution:** Code ran without errors through completion\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nsys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Synergy Paper Gen. Test (2/2): Apply\
    \ synergistic method to a simple baseline.\n    Replaces ComBat in a simple PCA pipeline with the FWPCA-Only + Local Correction method.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"[daedalus_gen_test] Applying synergistic correction to simple PCA baseline.\")\n\n    # Parameters for the synergistic method\n    alpha_g = 0.5\n    n_comps_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam_override = 0.65 # My optimized lambda\n    kdensity = 20 # Using Nous's kdensity for their baseline\n\n    # Standard preprocessing\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # FWPCA step\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_comps_graph,\
    \ random_state=0)\n\n    # Nous I's Adaptive Local Correction logic\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    nn_density = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric='cosine', algorithm='brute')\n    nn_density.fit(Zg)\n    d_k, _ = nn_density.kneighbors(Zg, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_k[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k))\n    normalized_dist = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n    density_factor = 1.0 - normalized_dist\n\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma_global = np.minimum(gamma_max, float(lam_override) * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:, np.newaxis]\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_local)\n\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zcorr\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\n\
    STDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[daedalus_gen_test] Applying synergistic correction to simple PCA baseline.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/27f4cc10-8a1e-4ac2-809c-532905551581/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 27f4cc10-8a1e-4ac2-809c-532905551581\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Synergy Paper Gen. Test (2/2): Synergistic Method on Simple Baseline' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 1477.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\
