tick: 1052
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have corrected the missing import in my generalization test script. The failure of the experiment, however, reveals a deeper issue. My synergistic method, while powerful on a complex DAQB-based pipeline, does not generalize to a simple embedding-only baseline. This is a critical negative result.\n\nI cannot publish my paper as is. I need to rethink my contribution. The synergy I found is real and high-scoring, but it's context-dependent. This is a valuable finding in itself.\n\nI will pivot my paper. Instead of presenting a new universal method, I will present a paper analyzing the *context-dependency* of this synergy. This aligns perfectly with the spirit of methodical analysis that defines my lineage.\n\n**New Paper Plan:**\n1.  **Frame:** The paper will investigate why the synergy between FWPCA-Only and Local Correction fails to generalize to a simple embedding baseline.\n2.  **Hypothesis:** The synergy relies on the DAQB graph construction step, which was absent in my failed\
    \ test.\n3.  **Experiment:** I will run one final experiment: apply my synergistic method, but this time, also include the DAQB graph construction step on top of the corrected embedding. If this succeeds, it proves the dependency on the graph.\n4.  **Rewrite:** I will rewrite my paper (Capsule #22) to reflect this new, more nuanced finding.\n\nFirst, I will prepare the script for this final, crucial experiment.\n\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/synergy_gen_test3_with_graph.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scipy.sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\n  from praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  def _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32)\
    \ + 1e-8\n      w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n      return Xd * w\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Synergy Dependency Test: Adds DAQB graph construction to the simple baseline.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"[daedalus_dependency_test] Applying synergistic correction AND DAQB graph to simple PCA baseline.\")\n      \n      alpha_g = 0.5\n      n_comps_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam_override = 0.65\n      kdensity = 18 # My optimized param\n      delta = 0.08  # My optimized param\n      k_total = 50\n      \n      normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\
    \n      Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n      Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_comps_graph, random_state=0)\n\n      B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      nn_density = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric='cosine', algorithm='brute')\n      nn_density.fit(Zg)\n      d_k, _ = nn_density.kneighbors(Zg, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_k[:, -1]\n      d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k))\n      normalized_dist = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      density_factor = 1.0 - normalized_dist\n      \n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma_global = np.minimum(gamma_max, float(lam_override) * R2).astype(np.float32)\n      gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:, np.newaxis]\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_local)\n      \n      #\
    \ Set embedding AND build graph\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zcorr\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=k_total, metric='cosine',\n                                           delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                           rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      \n      return adata\n```"
